#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-replay — score a CANDIDATE lander against a recorded set of past landings, offline, in one number.

TODAY'S LANDER (the core/lander package):
  cc-replay extract --lander [--repo R]... [--since STAMP] [--until STAMP] --out FILE
      A v3 trace from the lander's queue.log (`stage` lines and the requests) and its job files (live, or rest/):
      each PR first queued in the window, its requests and when history's lane first acted on each, its heads,
      every check it ran (head, secs, yes/no/main-red) and every verdict, its plan, files, conflicts and a
      branch gone, plus history's 1-minute load (sysstat) and its slot waits: each time a check started 1-60 min
      after the lane's `checking` line (or the check before it). A PR already in flight when the window opened is
      left out.
  cc-replay score --candidate DIR --trace V3 [--slots N] [--pickup history|arrival] [--verbose] [--keep]
      DIR is a tree holding core/lander (a checkout at a ref, a worktree, a release) or the package's directory.
      Its own Lane runs each repo's arrivals on a virtual clock, one repo at a time. The world stands in for git,
      GitHub, the manifest, the runner, the reviewer, the laptop (never reachable), the cards, the board, the tip
      and the deploy: a check returns the k-th result history recorded for it on that head after its recorded
      secs (main-red while history had that check red on main, anywhere); a check waits for a box-wide slot, as
      the runner's flock does, until fewer than the candidate's own slots_now() are busy — history's checks of the
      other repos and the replay's own, plus, during one of history's slot waits, the slots history's own checks
      left to work it never saw (a worker's own check run) — where slots_now() reads history's load; a review
      returns the verdict history recorded for that head; a conflict or a gone branch comes when history found
      it. --pickup history delivers each request when history's lane first acted on it (older releases left some
      untouched for hours); `arrival` delivers it when it was made. --slots sets the candidate's LANDER_SLOTS.
      Prints queued→merged p50 and p95 and the lane-minutes full-suite PRs held, history's same numbers beside
      them over the PRs both merged, then a per-PR table. The replay's own queue.log is read by the same parser.

THE OLD SINGLE-FILE LANDING TOOL (before the lander cut over):
  cc-replay extract [--repo R]... [--since STAMP] [--until STAMP] --out FILE
      Build the trace: which PRs were queued when, what their gates and reviews answered, how long they took,
      what a repair round pushed and when. Read from the landing queue's own ledger (queue.log), the sweeps'
      journal (journalctl --user), the gate logs under $TMPDIR, the reviewer transcripts, and `gh pr view`.
      Reads only. Writes a v2 trace and prints its event counts, then what it could not recover and how the gap was filled.
  cc-replay extract --from OLD --out FILE
      Make a v1 trace v2 without re-reading what may be gone since (gate logs, transcripts): add the three event
      classes from the journal and the checkout's own objects, keep the rest as it was read then.
  cc-replay score --candidate PATH --trace FILE [--conflicts history|files|none] [--verbose] [--keep]
      PATH must be a copy of the OLD single-file landing tool (`cc-bin-at <ref>` before the lander cut over). The
      file at core/bin of today is a shim onto the lander package, and it is refused with one line saying so.
      Import PATH as a module, stand the world in for it from the trace, and drive its own `queue` and `work`
      commands through the trace's arrivals on a VIRTUAL clock: a gate or a review parks its thread until the
      clock reaches its recorded duration, and the clock advances to the earliest wake only when every live
      thread is parked. No real gate, gh, git, systemd or Slack call is made; the candidate's own state lives
      under a temp root this tool creates and removes. Prints one score line and a per-PR table; the same
      input prints the same bytes every time. --verbose writes the world's log and the candidate's own output to
      stderr; --keep leaves the temp root in place to read afterwards.
  cc-replay selfcheck
      The virtual clock, the conflict model, the trace loader, determinism, the three v2 event classes, and a v3
      extract and score driving this checkout's own core/lander, on fixtures of its own.

THE OLD TOOL'S SCORE is the median minutes from a PR's first `queued` to its merge in the replay, over the PRs that merged;
suites run, paid reviews bought, repair rounds dispatched and PRs left unmerged are the secondary columns. A
`history` line gives history's median over the PRs both merged, for calibration. The per-PR table's last column
says how history merged each PR: `queue` (the landing queue did) or `hand` (a person did, outside it — on a v1
trace the replay lands one of those only where a LAND was recorded; on v2 see TRACE V2).

WHAT THE WORLD ANSWERS, and from where:
  · a gate returns its recorded rc after its recorded duration for that PR (else the trace median for that gate);
    a gate history saw go red at that head goes red here;
  · a review returns the verdict history recorded for that head (else for that change, else the PR's eventual
    verdict) after that PR's recorded review duration (else the median); a verdict a PERSON recorded (`cc-land
    record`) appears on the PR at its recorded time, written in the candidate's own marker format, and a recorded
    LAND queues the PR again when the replay had already given up on it (in history the job was still waiting,
    or the person queued it again — nobody types that in a replay); a PR history merged with no verdict on its
    last head is read as LAND there;
  · a repair round pushes the next recorded head after that PR's recorded fix latency (else the median);
  · mergeability is a MODEL: a PR conflicts when a PR merged since its base, in the REPLAY's order, touches one
    of its files (--conflicts files). Files overlap far more often than hunks do, so the default, `history`,
    applies that rule only to PRs history saw conflict; `none` never conflicts;
  · green records history spent are seeded for every head of the PR they were spent on, from its first arrival;
  · git is answered from the trace — file lists, per-file churn, a synthetic merge-base and diff per change —
    never from a checkout, so a decision that needs file CONTENTS (comment-only detection) reads every file as code.

TRACE V2 adds three event classes, and on a v2 trace (only there: a v1 trace scores to the bytes it always did):
  · memo: each landing's memo hits and misses, as history's journal recorded them. Extraction reads them — they
    are what those sweeps did — but nothing scores them: a candidate with no prepare phase files no memo, and
    report line 2 counts none. The plumbing behind them stays (rev-parse X^{commit}, merge-base --is-ancestor,
    merge-tree, commit-tree, rev-list --count, answered from content sets): the stops below are built on it;
  · stops: a landing stopped `behind` or on a `conflict`, with its head and how far behind the base it stood.
    `conflicted` counts only real conflicts; a PR stopped merely behind is refused by `gh pr merge` with GitHub's
    `--auto` words whenever the replay has it behind at all (`behind-refused`), and `gh pr update-branch` merges
    the base in: a new head, the same change, UPDATE_SECS on the clock (`base-updates`);
  · person: a PR a person merged outside the queue merges at that time (`person-merged`) unless the candidate
    lands it first. The median then covers those PRs too, so a v2 score is not comparable with a v1 score.

WHAT IT CANNOT SCORE: a suite made faster or slower, a reviewer made better or worse, or anything that depends on
what a file contains rather than which files changed. It scores the LANDING — order, parallelism, what is bought,
what is re-run, what is refused — on the same PRs, for two cc-lands.

Stdlib only. The code holds no repo names, PR numbers or paths of any one box; the trace is data and lives
outside the repo (~/.cc/state/<repo>/replay/ is the suggested home).
"""
import calendar, contextlib, glob, hashlib, heapq, importlib.machinery, importlib.util, inspect, io, json, os, re, shutil, statistics
import subprocess, sys, tempfile, threading, time

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
LANDQ = f"{HOME}/.cc/state/land"
BOARDS = f"{HOME}/.cc/boards"
GATES = ("core/tests/check.sh", "tests/check.sh", "tests/check-extra.sh", "core/tests/selftest.sh", "tests/selftest.sh")
SUITE = ("core/tests/selftest.sh", "tests/selftest.sh")
CONTROL_LIST = ("core/tests/control-layer", "tests/control-layer")
VERDICTS = ("LAND", "LAND-AFTER-FIX", "DO-NOT-LAND")
REVIEW_MODEL_RE = re.compile(r"^claude-")        # a verdict signed by a model was BOUGHT by a landing; any other name recorded it
DEFAULTS = {"gate": {"check.sh": 120, "check-extra.sh": 180, "selftest.sh": 900}, "review": 480, "fix": 1500}
GATE_MIN, GATE_MAX = 20, 4 * 3600               # a log span outside this is not one run of one gate
GATE_SPAN_CAP = 3                               # nor is one past this many times the gate's median
UPDATE_SECS = 30                                # v2: what `gh pr update-branch` takes; nothing recorded it


def stamp(e):
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(e))


def epoch(s):
    try:
        return calendar.timegm(time.strptime(s or "", "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"))
    except ValueError:
        return 0


def iso_epoch(s):
    """An ISO stamp with any offset (journalctl -o short-iso, gh) as an epoch; 0 when unreadable."""
    from datetime import datetime
    try:
        return int(datetime.fromisoformat(s.replace("Z", "+00:00")).timestamp())
    except (ValueError, AttributeError):
        return 0


def read_json(path):
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            return json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def sh(argv, cwd=None, timeout=120):
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(argv, cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        return r.returncode, r.stdout + r.stderr
    except Exception as e:
        return 127, f"{e.__class__.__name__}: {e}"


def median(xs, default):
    xs = [x for x in xs if x]
    return statistics.median(xs) if xs else default


def hexname(*parts):
    return hashlib.sha256("\0".join(str(p) for p in parts).encode()).hexdigest()[:40]


# ── extract ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LEDGER_RE = re.compile(r"^(?P<at>\S+)\t(?P<kind>[a-z-]+) (?P<repo>[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)#(?P<pr>[0-9]+|deploy)(?P<rest>.*)$")
MARK_OLD = re.compile(r"\A\s*<!-- cc-land-review ([0-9a-f]{7,40}) (LAND-AFTER-FIX|DO-NOT-LAND|LAND) -->")
MARK_V2 = re.compile(r"\A\s*<!-- cc-land-review v2 change=([0-9a-f]+)(?: base=([0-9a-f]+))? head=([0-9a-f]+) "
                     r"verdict=(LAND-AFTER-FIX|DO-NOT-LAND|LAND)(?: by=([A-Za-z0-9._@-]+))?[^>]*-->")
JOURNAL_RE = re.compile(r"^(?P<at>\S+) \S+ cc-land\[(?P<pid>\d+)\]: (?P<text>.*)$")


def repo_root_of(repo):
    p = (read_json(f"{BOARDS}/{repo}.json") or {}).get("path") or ""
    return p if p and os.path.isdir(f"{p}/.git") else f"{HOME}/dev/{repo}"


def ledger_events(path, since, until):
    out = []
    try:
        lines = open(path, errors="replace").read().splitlines()
    except OSError:
        return out
    for ln in lines:
        m = LEDGER_RE.match(ln)
        if not m or m.group("pr") == "deploy":
            continue
        at = epoch(m.group("at"))
        if not at or at < since or at > until:
            continue
        out.append({"at": at, "kind": m.group("kind"), "repo": m.group("repo"), "pr": int(m.group("pr")),
                    "rest": m.group("rest").strip()})
    return out


def gh_pr(repo, pr, cache=""):
    """What GitHub says about the PR; a merged or closed PR's answer is kept beside the trace, so a second
    extraction does not ask again."""
    cached = f"{cache}/{repo}-{pr}.json" if cache else ""
    if cached and os.path.exists(cached):
        return read_json(cached)
    rc, o = sh(["gh", "pr", "view", str(pr), "--json", "number,title,state,createdAt,mergedAt,closedAt,headRefOid,"
                "headRefName,baseRefName,additions,deletions,files,comments,mergeCommit"], cwd=repo_root_of(repo))
    if rc:
        return None
    try:
        j = json.loads(o)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    if cached and j.get("state") in ("MERGED", "CLOSED"):
        os.makedirs(cache, exist_ok=True)
        with open(cached, "w") as f:
            json.dump(j, f)
    return j


HUNK = re.compile(r"^@@ -[0-9,]+ \+[0-9,]+ @@.*$")    # the whole header, function-context tail too: the landing's v2 key
HUNK_LEGACY = re.compile(r"^@@ -[0-9,]+ \+[0-9,]+ @@")  # the tail kept: the key a verdict written before 2026-09-19 carries


def change_digest(diff, legacy=False):
    """The landing's own change key, kept in step with it: the diff text with the `index` lines and the hunk header
    dropped (its numbers and, unless `legacy`, the function-context tail), hashed. Two heads with the same digest
    are one change (a rebase between them)."""
    keep = []
    for ln in (diff or "").splitlines():
        if ln.startswith("index "):
            continue
        keep.append((HUNK_LEGACY if legacy else HUNK).sub("@@", ln) if ln.startswith("@@ ") else ln)
    body = "\n".join(keep).strip()
    return hashlib.sha256(body.encode("utf-8", "replace")).hexdigest()[:40] if body else ""


def change_key_of(root, base, sha, legacy=False):
    """The change a head IS, read from the checkout's own objects — read-only, and "" when the head is not there.
    merge-base against the base branch as it stands: the fork point of an old head does not move."""
    rc, o = sh(["git", "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", f"{sha}^{{commit}}"], cwd=root)
    if rc:
        return ""
    full = o.strip()
    rc, o = sh(["git", "merge-base", f"origin/{base}", full], cwd=root)
    if rc or not o.strip():
        return ""
    r = subprocess.run(["git", "diff", "-U3", o.strip().split()[0], full], cwd=root, capture_output=True, text=True)
    return change_digest(r.stdout, legacy) if r.returncode == 0 else ""


def same_change(a, b):
    """Two heads' key sets name one change when they share a key: a marker may carry either rule's key."""
    return bool((set(a) & set(b)) - {""})


def journal_lines(since):
    rc, o = sh(["journalctl", "--user", "--no-pager", "-o", "short-iso", "--since", f"@{since}"], timeout=300)
    if rc:
        return []
    out = []
    for ln in o.splitlines():
        m = JOURNAL_RE.match(ln)
        if m:
            out.append((iso_epoch(m.group("at")), int(m.group("pid")), m.group("text")))
    return out


GATE_LINE = re.compile(r"(\d+) gate\(s\) passed on PR #(\d+)(?: at the (\w+) tier)?[^:]*: (.*?)(?: — (\d+) of them already green on ([0-9a-f]+))?(?: —|;|$)")
GREEN_LINE = re.compile(r"^\s*· (\S+): already green on this content \(([0-9a-f]+)\)")
TIER_LINE = re.compile(r"^\s*· the (\w+) tier: ")
NOMODEL_LINE = re.compile(r"no model read this diff — the (\w+) tier")
BOUGHT_LINE = re.compile(r"reviewed by (\S+) at the (\w+) tier .*?: (LAND-AFTER-FIX|DO-NOT-LAND|LAND) on PR #(\d+) \(\$([0-9.]+)")
STOP_BOUGHT = re.compile(r"✗ review: (LAND-AFTER-FIX|DO-NOT-LAND|LAND) on PR #(\d+) \(\$([0-9.]+)")
READ_LINE = re.compile(r"read already by (\S+): (LAND-AFTER-FIX|DO-NOT-LAND|LAND) on PR #(\d+)")
MERGED_LINE = re.compile(r"✓ PR #(\d+) merged \(")       # the queue's own merge; "already merged — nothing to do" is a hand merge it noticed
LANDING_LINE = re.compile(r"^landing \[([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)\] PR #(\d+)")


def journal_facts(lines):
    """Per (repo, pr): the tier each landing ran at, which gates a green record answered for, and whether the
    review was bought, read back or skipped — from the lines the sweeps printed. A job's lines name the PR in
    the gate and review lines; the `already green` lines just before a gate line belong to that gate line."""
    facts = {}
    pending, repo_of = {}, {}

    def f(repo, pr):
        return facts.setdefault((repo, pr), {"tiers": [], "green": [], "bought": [], "read": [], "nomodel": [], "queue_merged": False})

    for at, pid, text in lines:
        m = LANDING_LINE.match(text)
        if m:
            repo_of[pid] = m.group(1)
        m = GREEN_LINE.match(text)
        if m:
            pending.setdefault(pid, []).append(m.group(1))
            continue
        m = GATE_LINE.search(text)
        if m:
            pr = int(m.group(2))
            repo = repo_of.get(pid) or repo_of_pr(pr, facts)
            if repo:
                rec = f(repo, pr)
                if m.group(3):
                    rec["tiers"].append((at, m.group(3)))
                for g in pending.pop(pid, []):
                    rec["green"].append((at, g))
            else:
                pending.pop(pid, None)
            continue
        m = BOUGHT_LINE.search(text) or STOP_BOUGHT.search(text)
        if m:
            g = m.groups()
            verdict, pr, cost = (g[2], int(g[3]), float(g[4])) if len(g) == 5 else (g[0], int(g[1]), float(g[2]))
            repo = repo_of.get(pid) or repo_of_pr(pr, facts)
            if repo:
                f(repo, pr)["bought"].append((at, verdict, cost))
            continue
        m = READ_LINE.search(text)
        if m:
            repo = repo_of.get(pid) or repo_of_pr(int(m.group(3)), facts)
            if repo:
                f(repo, int(m.group(3)))["read"].append((at, m.group(2), m.group(1)))
            continue
        m = MERGED_LINE.search(text)
        if m:
            repo = repo_of.get(pid) or repo_of_pr(int(m.group(1)), facts)
            if repo:
                f(repo, int(m.group(1)))["queue_merged"] = True
            continue
        m = NOMODEL_LINE.search(text)
        if m and repo_of.get(pid):
            pass    # the tier line above already carries the tier; nothing to add
    return facts


def repo_of_pr(pr, facts):
    hits = {r for (r, p) in facts if p == pr}
    return hits.pop() if len(hits) == 1 else ""


# ── trace v2: the three event classes v1 could not see ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
PREPARE_HEADER = re.compile(r"^gating and reading \d+ queued job")
STOP_BEHIND = re.compile(r"is not mergeable yet|base branch policy prohibits")
STOP_CONFLICT = re.compile(r"conflicts with \S+ — rebase|merge conflicts")


def memo_facts(lines, prs):
    """{(repo, pr): [(at, hit)]} — whether a sweep's serial walk spent the gate memo its own prepare phase left. A
    hit prints `run for this sweep by the prepare phase`; a miss is a PR whose gates passed twice in one sweep that
    ran a prepare phase, once in the pool and once again in the walk (a sweep is one process, so one pid). A walk
    that missed its memo and then went red is not counted: the red line does not say which phase ran it."""
    out, passes, prep, repo_of = {}, {}, set(), {}
    for at, pid, text in lines:
        m = LANDING_LINE.match(text)
        if m:
            repo_of[pid] = m.group(1)
        if PREPARE_HEADER.match(text):
            prep.add(pid)
        m = GATE_LINE.search(text)
        if not m:
            continue
        pr = int(m.group(2))
        repo = repo_of.get(pid) if (repo_of.get(pid), pr) in prs else repo_of_pr(pr, dict.fromkeys(prs))
        if not repo:
            continue
        if "by the prepare phase" in text:
            out.setdefault((repo, pr), []).append((at, True))
        elif m.group(3):
            passes.setdefault((pid, repo, pr), []).append(at)
    for (pid, repo, pr), ats in passes.items():
        if pid in prep and len(ats) >= 2:
            out.setdefault((repo, pr), []).append((max(ats), False))
    return out


def behind_by(root, base, head, at):
    """How many commits the base held at `at` that `head` did not, read from the checkout's own objects — read-only,
    None when a head or the base at that time is not there."""
    rc, o = sh(["git", "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", f"{head}^{{commit}}"], cwd=root)
    if rc:
        return None
    full = o.strip()
    rc, o = sh(["git", "rev-list", "-1", f"--before=@{at}", f"origin/{base}"], cwd=root)
    if rc or not o.strip():
        return None
    rc, o = sh(["git", "rev-list", "--count", f"{full}..{o.strip()}"], cwd=root)
    return int(o.strip()) if rc == 0 and o.strip().isdigit() else None


def stops_of(l, root):
    """The landings history stopped short of the merge on mergeability, not on a gate: `behind` (GitHub refused the
    merge, the queue printed "not mergeable yet") or `conflict`, each with the head it stood on and how far behind
    the base that head was then."""
    out = []
    for d in l.get("dones") or []:
        if re.search(r"gate \S+ did not pass", d["short"]):
            continue
        kind = "behind" if STOP_BEHIND.search(d["short"]) else "conflict" if STOP_CONFLICT.search(d["short"]) else ""
        if kind:
            at = epoch(d["at"])
            head = next((h["sha"] for h in reversed(l["heads"]) if epoch(h["at"]) <= at), l["heads"][0]["sha"])
            out.append({"at": d["at"], "kind": kind, "head": head, "behind": behind_by(root, l.get("base") or "main", head, at)})
    return out


def upgrade(trace, lines):
    """A v1 trace made v2, in place: each landing gains `memo` (history's memo hits and misses), `stops` (its
    mergeability stops) and `person` (the time a person merged it outside the queue, or null); `conflicted` is
    re-read from the stops, so a PR merely behind is no longer counted as one that conflicted."""
    until = epoch(trace.get("until")) or int(time.time())
    prs = {(l["repo"], l["pr"]) for l in trace["landings"]}
    memo = memo_facts([ln for ln in lines if ln[0] <= until], prs)
    for l in trace["landings"]:
        l["memo"] = [{"at": stamp(at), "hit": hit} for at, hit in sorted(memo.get((l["repo"], l["pr"]), []))]
        l["stops"] = stops_of(l, repo_root_of(l["repo"]))
        l["conflicted"] = any(s["kind"] == "conflict" for s in l["stops"])
        l["person"] = {"at": l["merged"]} if l.get("merged") and not l.get("queue_merged") else None
    ls = trace["landings"]
    counts = {"memo_hits": sum(m["hit"] for l in ls for m in l["memo"]),
              "memo_misses": sum(not m["hit"] for l in ls for m in l["memo"]),
              "stops_behind": sum(s["kind"] == "behind" for l in ls for s in l["stops"]),
              "stops_conflict": sum(s["kind"] == "conflict" for l in ls for s in l["stops"]),
              "person": sum(1 for l in ls if l["person"])}
    gaps = [g for g in trace.get("gaps") or [] if not re.search(r"conflicted in history|merged OUTSIDE the queue", g)]
    gaps.append(f"{sum(1 for l in ls if l['conflicted'])} PRs conflicted in history and "
                f"{sum(1 for l in ls if any(s['kind'] == 'behind' for s in l['stops']))} were stopped merely behind; "
                f"--conflicts history conflicts only the first, and only the second are refused as behind")
    gaps.append(f"{sum(1 for l in ls for s in l['stops'] if s['behind'] is None)} of "
                f"{counts['stops_behind'] + counts['stops_conflict']} stops have no distance behind (the head or the "
                f"base of that hour is not in the checkout)")
    gaps.append(f"{counts['person']} PRs a person merged outside the queue merge in the replay at their history "
                f"time, unless the candidate lands them first")
    gaps.append("a memo the serial walk missed and then went red on is not in `memo`: the red line does not name its phase")
    trace.update(version=2, counts=counts, gaps=gaps)
    return counts


def gate_log_spans(tmpdir):
    """{(repo, pr, gate-basename): seconds} from each gate log's birth to its last write. The file is truncated and
    rewritten on every run of that gate for that PR, and truncation keeps the inode, so the span covers EVERY run:
    only a PR gated once can be read off it, and the caller decides that. Since 2026-09-11 a log lives under its
    run's root, `<tmp>/cc-land.run.<pid>.<random>/`, and a green run takes its logs with it when it ends: what is
    on disk to read is a run still going and the log of a gate that went red. Logs at the old place, straight
    under the temp root, are read too while any remain."""
    out = {}
    for p in glob.glob(f"{tmpdir}/cc-land-gate-*.log") + glob.glob(f"{tmpdir}/cc-land.run.*/cc-land-gate-*.log"):
        m = re.match(r"cc-land-gate-(.+)-(\d+|base)-([^-]+\.sh)\.log$", os.path.basename(p))
        if not m or m.group(2) == "base":
            continue
        rc, o = sh(["stat", "-c", "%W %Y", p])
        try:
            birth, mtime = (int(x) for x in o.split())
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if birth > 0 and mtime > birth:
            out[(m.group(1), int(m.group(2)), m.group(3))] = mtime - birth
    return out


def review_spans():
    """{(repo, pr): [seconds...]} — how long each paid review of that PR ran, from the reviewer's own transcript:
    it runs in a directory named cc-land.review.<repo>.<pr>.<random>, and the transcript's first and last stamps
    bracket the read."""
    out = {}
    for d in glob.glob(f"{HOME}/.claude/projects/-tmp-cc-land-review-*"):
        m = re.match(r"-tmp-cc-land-review-(.+)-(\d+)-[A-Za-z0-9]+$", os.path.basename(d))
        if not m:
            continue
        stamps = []
        for j in glob.glob(f"{d}/*.jsonl"):
            try:
                for ln in open(j, errors="replace"):
                    mm = re.search(r'"timestamp":"([^"]+)"', ln)
                    if mm:
                        stamps.append(iso_epoch(mm.group(1)))
            except OSError:
                pass
        stamps = [s for s in stamps if s]
        if len(stamps) >= 2 and 10 <= max(stamps) - min(stamps) <= 3 * 3600:
            out.setdefault((m.group(1), int(m.group(2))), []).append(max(stamps) - min(stamps))
    return out


def parse_marker(body):
    """(head12, verdict, change-key, by, kind) from a review comment, or None."""
    m = MARK_V2.match(body or "")
    if m:
        key, head, verdict, by = m.group(1), m.group(3), m.group(4), m.group(5) or ""
    else:
        m = MARK_OLD.match(body or "")
        if not m:
            return None
        head, verdict, key, by = m.group(1), m.group(2), "", ""
    if not by:
        mm = re.search(r"(?:read by|model) `([^`]+)`", body)
        by = mm.group(1) if mm else ""
    kind = "bought" if (not by or REVIEW_MODEL_RE.match(by)) else "recorded"
    return head[:12], verdict, key, by, kind


def build_landing(repo, pr, events, gh, jf, spans, rspans, until):
    """One PR's record, from every source that mentions it."""
    ev = sorted(events, key=lambda e: (e["at"], e["kind"]))
    arrivals = [{"at": stamp(e["at"]), "again": e["kind"] == "again"} for e in ev if e["kind"] in ("queued", "again")]
    dones = []
    for e in ev:
        if e["kind"] == "done":
            m = re.match(r"rc=(\d+) (.*)", e["rest"])
            if m:
                dones.append({"at": stamp(e["at"]), "rc": int(m.group(1)), "short": m.group(2)[:240]})
    fixes, open_fix = [], None
    for e in ev:
        if e["kind"] == "fix-dispatch":
            m = re.search(r"track=(\S+).*head=([0-9a-f]+)", e["rest"])
            open_fix = {"dispatched": stamp(e["at"]), "track": m.group(1) if m else "", "old": m.group(2)[:12] if m else ""}
            fixes.append(open_fix)
        elif e["kind"] == "fix-pushed" and open_fix and "pushed" not in open_fix:
            m = re.search(r"([0-9a-f]{7,40})->([0-9a-f]{7,40})", e["rest"])
            open_fix.update(pushed=stamp(e["at"]), old=m.group(1)[:12] if m else open_fix["old"], new=m.group(2)[:12] if m else "")
    # Every head anyone saw, with when: the comment markers, the ledger's recorded/fix lines, and the head the
    # PR ends on. Ordered by first sighting; a head pushed by a repair round is a NEW change, a head with the same
    # change key as the one before it is a rebase, and a head with no key and no repair between is read as a
    # rebase too — the caveat is in the docs.
    sightings = {}       # sha12 -> (at, via, key)

    def see(sha, at, via="push", key=""):
        sha = (sha or "")[:12]
        if not sha:
            return
        if sha not in sightings or at < sightings[sha][0]:
            sightings[sha] = (at, via, key or (sightings.get(sha) or ("", "", ""))[2])

    created = iso_epoch(gh.get("createdAt") or "") if gh else 0
    verdicts = []
    for c in (gh or {}).get("comments") or []:
        if not isinstance(c, dict) or not c.get("viewerDidAuthor"):
            continue
        pm = parse_marker(c.get("body") or "")
        if not pm:
            continue
        head, verdict, key, by, kind = pm
        at = iso_epoch(c.get("createdAt") or "")
        see(head, at - (median(rspans.get((repo, pr), []), DEFAULTS["review"]) if kind == "bought" else 0), key=key)
        cost = 0.0
        for bat, bverdict, bcost in jf.get("bought", []):
            if bverdict == verdict and abs(bat - at) < 120:
                cost = bcost
        verdicts.append({"at": stamp(at), "head": head, "verdict": verdict, "by": by, "kind": kind, "cost": cost})
    for e in ev:
        if e["kind"] == "recorded":
            m = re.match(r"(LAND-AFTER-FIX|DO-NOT-LAND|LAND) by=(\S+) head=([0-9a-f]+) change=(\S+)", e["rest"])
            if m:
                see(m.group(3), e["at"], key="" if m.group(4) == "-" else m.group(4))
                if not any(v["head"] == m.group(3)[:12] and v["verdict"] == m.group(1) for v in verdicts):
                    verdicts.append({"at": stamp(e["at"]), "head": m.group(3)[:12], "verdict": m.group(1),
                                     "by": m.group(2), "kind": "recorded", "cost": 0.0})
        elif e["kind"] == "stale-pull-ref":
            for sha in re.findall(r"=([0-9a-f]{7,40})", e["rest"]):
                see(sha, e["at"])
    for fx in fixes:
        see(fx.get("old"), epoch(fx["dispatched"]) - 1)
        if fx.get("new"):
            see(fx["new"], epoch(fx["pushed"]), via="fix")
    for d in dones:       # a stop names the head it stopped on; that head was there when the attempt was queued
        before = [epoch(a["at"]) for a in arrivals if epoch(a["at"]) <= epoch(d["at"])]
        for sha in re.findall(r"\b[0-9a-f]{12}\b", d["short"]):
            see(sha, before[-1] if before else epoch(d["at"]))
    final = ((gh or {}).get("headRefOid") or "")[:12]
    if final:
        merged_at = iso_epoch((gh or {}).get("mergedAt") or "") or until
        see(final, merged_at - 30)
    if not sightings:
        see(hexname(repo, pr, "head0"), created or (epoch(arrivals[0]["at"]) if arrivals else 0))
    order = sorted(sightings.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1][0])
    root, base = repo_root_of(repo), (gh or {}).get("baseRefName") or "main"
    heads, gen, last_key, last_keys, keyed = [], 0, None, (), 0
    for i, (sha, (at, via, key)) in enumerate(order):
        key = key or change_key_of(root, base, sha)      # the checkout's objects settle it where the marker did not
        keys = (key, change_key_of(root, base, sha), change_key_of(root, base, sha, legacy=True)) if key else ()
        if key and (i == 0 or sightings[order[i - 1][0]][2] or True):
            keyed += 1
        if i:
            if via == "fix":
                gen += 1
            elif key and last_key:
                gen += 0 if same_change(keys, last_keys) else 1
            # no key on either side: a rebase — see the caveats
        heads.append({"at": stamp(max(at, 0)), "sha": sha, "gen": gen, "via": via if i else "push", "key": key[:12]})
        last_key, last_keys = key or last_key, keys or last_keys
    unkeyed = sum(1 for h in heads if not h["key"])
    heads[0]["at"] = stamp(min(epoch(heads[0]["at"]), created or epoch(heads[0]["at"]),
                              epoch(arrivals[0]["at"]) if arrivals else epoch(heads[0]["at"])))

    def gen_at(at):
        g = 0
        for h in heads:
            if epoch(h["at"]) <= at:
                g = h["gen"]
        return g

    for v in verdicts:
        v["gen"] = next((h["gen"] for h in heads if h["sha"] == v["head"]), gen_at(epoch(v["at"])))
    red, conflicted = {}, False
    for d in dones:
        m = re.search(r"gate (\S+) did not pass", d["short"])
        if m:       # keyed by the HEAD it went red on: the rebase that fixed PR #305's stale red is a new head
            head_then = next((h["sha"] for h in reversed(heads) if epoch(h["at"]) <= epoch(d["at"])), heads[0]["sha"])
            red.setdefault(os.path.basename(m.group(1)), []).append(head_then)
        if re.search(r"conflicts with|merge conflicts|not mergeable", d["short"]):
            conflicted = True
    files = [[("A" if f.get("additions") and not f.get("deletions") and f.get("changeType") == "ADDED" else "M"), f["path"]]
             for f in (gh or {}).get("files") or [] if isinstance(f, dict) and f.get("path")]
    perfile = {f["path"]: [f.get("additions") or 0, f.get("deletions") or 0]
               for f in (gh or {}).get("files") or [] if isinstance(f, dict) and f.get("path")}
    attempts = len(dones) + (1 if arrivals and (not dones or epoch(arrivals[-1]["at"]) > epoch(dones[-1]["at"])) else 0)
    gates = {}      # one arrival AND one head: a repair push or a rebase re-runs the gates into the same log
    for (r, p, g), secs in spans.items():
        if (r, p) == (repo, pr) and attempts <= 1 and len(heads) <= 1 and GATE_MIN <= secs <= GATE_MAX:
            gates[g] = secs
    green = sorted({os.path.basename(g) for _, g in jf.get("green", [])})
    tiers = sorted({t for _, t in jf.get("tiers", [])})
    return {"repo": repo, "pr": pr, "title": (gh or {}).get("title") or "", "branch": (gh or {}).get("headRefName") or "",
            "base": (gh or {}).get("baseRefName") or "main", "created": stamp(created) if created else "",
            "merged": stamp(iso_epoch(gh["mergedAt"])) if gh and gh.get("mergedAt") else "",
            "state": (gh or {}).get("state") or "", "files": files, "perfile": perfile,
            "adds": (gh or {}).get("additions") or 0, "dels": (gh or {}).get("deletions") or 0,
            "arrivals": arrivals, "heads": heads, "verdicts": sorted(verdicts, key=lambda v: v["at"]),
            "fixes": fixes, "dones": dones, "gates": gates, "red": red, "green": green, "tiers": tiers,
            "review_secs": sorted(rspans.get((repo, pr), [])), "attempts": attempts, "conflicted": conflicted,
            "unkeyed_heads": unkeyed, "queue_merged": bool(jf.get("queue_merged"))}


def print_counts(out, trace):
    c = trace["counts"]
    print(f"wrote {out}: trace v{trace['version']}, {len(trace['landings'])} landings, "
          f"{sum(len(l['arrivals']) for l in trace['landings'])} arrivals")
    print(f"  memo: {c['memo_hits']} hit, {c['memo_misses']} missed · stops: {c['stops_behind']} behind, "
          f"{c['stops_conflict']} conflict · person merges: {c['person']}")


def cmd_extract(argv):
    repos, since, until, out, old, lander = [], 0, int(time.time()), "", "", False
    rest = list(argv)
    while rest:
        a = rest.pop(0)
        if a == "--lander":
            lander = True
        elif a == "--from" and rest:
            old = rest.pop(0)
        elif a == "--repo" and rest:
            repos.append(rest.pop(0))
        elif a == "--since" and rest:
            since = epoch(rest.pop(0))
        elif a == "--until" and rest:
            until = epoch(rest.pop(0))
        elif a == "--out" and rest:
            out = rest.pop(0)
        else:
            print(f"cc-replay extract: unexpected '{a}'", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    if not out:
        print("cc-replay extract: --out FILE is required", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if lander:
        landq = os.environ.get("CC_LANDER_STATE") or LANDQ
        trace = lander_trace(f"{landq}/queue.log", landq, since or until - 86400, until, repos)
        if not trace["prs"]:
            print("cc-replay extract: no PR first queued in that window", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(out)), exist_ok=True)
        with open(out, "w") as f:
            json.dump(trace, f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
        n = len(trace["prs"])
        print(f"{out}: {n} PR(s), {sum(len(p['arrivals']) for p in trace['prs'])} arrivals, "
              f"{sum(len(r) for p in trace['prs'] for r in p['gates'].values())} checks, "
              f"{sum(len(p['verdicts']) for p in trace['prs'])} reads, {sum(1 for p in trace['prs'] if p['merged'])} merged; "
              f"{len(trace['left_out'])} PR(s) first queued before the window left out")
        return 0
    if old:     # the v1 half is kept as it was read then: its gate spans and transcripts may be gone since
        trace = load_trace(old)
        upgrade(trace, journal_lines(epoch(trace["since"])))
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(out)), exist_ok=True)
        with open(out, "w") as f:
            json.dump(trace, f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
        print_counts(out, trace)
        return 0
    since = since or until - 86400
    events = ledger_events(f"{LANDQ}/queue.log", since, until)
    prs = sorted({(e["repo"], e["pr"]) for e in events if e["kind"] == "queued" and (not repos or e["repo"] in repos)})
    if not prs:
        print("cc-replay extract: no `queued` line in that window", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    print(f"extracting {len(prs)} PR(s) queued between {stamp(since)} and {stamp(until)}", file=sys.stderr)
    jlines = journal_lines(since)
    jf = journal_facts(jlines)
    spans = {}        # cc-land runs in ~/.cc/tmp since 2026-09-24; a caller whose TMPDIR predates that reads /tmp
    for d in dict.fromkeys([tempfile.gettempdir(), f"{HOME}/.cc/tmp"]):
        spans.update(gate_log_spans(d))
    rspans = review_spans()
    landings, gaps, missing_gh = [], [], []
    cache = f"{os.path.abspath(out)}.gh"
    for repo, pr in prs:
        gh = gh_pr(repo, pr, cache)
        if gh is None:
            missing_gh.append(f"{repo}#{pr}")
        mine = [e for e in events if (e["repo"], e["pr"]) == (repo, pr)]
        landings.append(build_landing(repo, pr, mine, gh, jf.get((repo, pr), {}), spans, rspans, until))
    repos_out = {}
    for repo in sorted({l["repo"] for l in landings}):
        root = repo_root_of(repo)
        gates = [g for g in GATES if os.access(f"{root}/{g}", os.X_OK)]
        control = None
        base = (read_json(f"{BOARDS}/{repo}.json") or {}).get("default_branch") or "main"
        for lst in CONTROL_LIST:
            rc, o = sh(["git", "show", f"origin/{base}:{lst}"], cwd=root)
            if rc == 0:
                control = (lst, o)
                break
        repos_out[repo] = {"default_branch": base, "gates": gates, "control": control}
    medians = {"gate": {}, "review": int(median([s for v in rspans.values() for s in v], DEFAULTS["review"])),
               "fix": int(median([epoch(f["pushed"]) - epoch(f["dispatched"]) for l in landings for f in l["fixes"]
                                  if f.get("pushed")], DEFAULTS["fix"]))}
    for g in sorted({g for l in landings for g in l["gates"]} | set(DEFAULTS["gate"])):
        medians["gate"][g] = int(median([l["gates"][g] for l in landings if g in l["gates"]], DEFAULTS["gate"].get(g, 300)))
    n_capped = 0    # a span past GATE_SPAN_CAP× the gate's median is a wait at a lock or two runs, not one run
    for l in landings:
        for g in [g for g, secs in l["gates"].items() if secs > GATE_SPAN_CAP * medians["gate"][g]]:
            del l["gates"][g]
            n_capped += 1
    for g in medians["gate"]:
        medians["gate"][g] = int(median([l["gates"][g] for l in landings if g in l["gates"]], medians["gate"][g]))
    # What could not be recovered, said plainly, and how the gap is filled.
    n_multi = sum(1 for l in landings if l["attempts"] > 1 or len(l["heads"]) > 1)
    n_nogate = sum(1 for l in landings if not l["gates"])
    n_norev = sum(1 for l in landings if not l["review_secs"])
    n_nohead = sum(1 for l in landings if len(l["heads"]) == 1 and l["heads"][0]["sha"] == hexname(l["repo"], l["pr"], "head0"))
    gaps.append(f"{n_multi} of {len(landings)} PRs were gated more than once (a second arrival, a repair push or a "
                f"rebase); their gate logs span every run, so their gate durations are the trace median per gate "
                f"({', '.join(f'{k} {v}s' for k, v in medians['gate'].items())}); {n_capped} more span(s) past "
                f"{GATE_SPAN_CAP}× that median (a wait at a lock is not a run) get the median too")
    gaps.append(f"{n_nogate} PRs have no usable gate log at all (never gated, or a green record answered) — median per gate")
    gaps.append(f"{n_norev} PRs have no reviewer transcript — review duration is the median {medians['review']}s")
    gaps.append(f"repair latency: {sum(1 for l in landings for f in l['fixes'] if f.get('pushed'))} rounds measured, "
                f"median {medians['fix']}s; a round with no measured push uses that")
    gaps.append(f"{n_nohead} PRs have no head anybody wrote down — one synthetic head, one change")
    n_unkeyed = sum(l.get("unkeyed_heads", 0) for l in landings)
    gaps.append(f"{n_unkeyed} of {sum(len(l['heads']) for l in landings)} heads have no change key (no marker, not in "
                f"the checkout): a move onto one is read as a rebase unless a repair round pushed it; the force-push "
                f"timeline (gh api) is not read here, so a head nobody wrote down is not in the trace at all")
    gaps.append(f"{sum(1 for l in landings if l.get('conflicted'))} PRs conflicted in history; the default conflict "
                f"model (--conflicts history) can only conflict those")
    gaps.append("review budgets spent BEFORE the window are not seeded: every change starts with none bought")
    n_hand = sum(1 for l in landings if l["merged"] and not l["queue_merged"])
    gaps.append(f"{n_hand} PRs history merged OUTSIDE the queue (a person merged, mostly after the review-budget wall; "
                f"hist-by=hand in the table): the replay lands one only where a LAND was recorded, and its history "
                f"minutes are a person's, not a queue's")
    if missing_gh:
        gaps.append(f"gh could not read {len(missing_gh)} PR(s) ({', '.join(missing_gh[:5])}): no files, no verdicts, "
                    f"treated as a one-file change with no history")
    trace = {"version": 1, "since": stamp(since), "until": stamp(until), "repos": repos_out, "medians": medians,
             "landings": landings, "gaps": gaps}
    upgrade(trace, jlines)
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(out)), exist_ok=True)
    with open(out, "w") as f:
        json.dump(trace, f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
    print_counts(out, trace)
    print("could not recover, and how it was filled:")
    for g in trace["gaps"]:
        print(f"  · {g}")
    return 0


def load_trace(path):
    t = read_json(path)
    if isinstance(t, dict) and t.get("version") == 3 and t.get("kind") == "lander" and isinstance(t.get("prs"), list):
        return t
    if not isinstance(t, dict) or t.get("version") not in (1, 2) or not isinstance(t.get("landings"), list):
        raise SystemExit(f"cc-replay: {path} is not a v1 or v2 trace")
    for l in t["landings"]:
        for k in ("repo", "pr", "arrivals", "heads", "files"):
            if k not in l:
                raise SystemExit(f"cc-replay: {path}: landing without '{k}'")
        l.setdefault("verdicts", []); l.setdefault("fixes", []); l.setdefault("gates", {}); l.setdefault("red", {})
        l.setdefault("green", []); l.setdefault("review_secs", []); l.setdefault("perfile", {}); l.setdefault("base", "main")
        l.setdefault("branch", ""); l.setdefault("merged", ""); l.setdefault("title", ""); l.setdefault("conflicted", False)
        l.setdefault("memo", []); l.setdefault("stops", []); l.setdefault("person", None)
    t.setdefault("medians", dict(DEFAULTS)); t["medians"].setdefault("gate", dict(DEFAULTS["gate"]))
    t["medians"].setdefault("review", DEFAULTS["review"]); t["medians"].setdefault("fix", DEFAULTS["fix"])
    t.setdefault("repos", {})
    return t


# ── the virtual clock, and the threading the candidate is handed ─────────────────────────────────────────
class Deadlock(Exception):
    pass


class Clock:
    """Discrete-event time. Every thread the candidate runs is counted RUNNING until it parks — in a stub that
    waits out a duration, in a join, in an Event or Condition wait. The clock moves only when nothing is
    running: the last thread to park advances it, to the earliest of the next trace arrival (which it injects)
    and the earliest parked wake, and marks the woken threads running before it blocks itself. The count
    therefore never sits at zero with work to do, and the same trace walks the same virtual times every run."""

    def __init__(self, now):
        self.now = now
        self.lock = threading.Lock()
        self.running = 1           # the driver
        self.sleepers = []         # (wake, seq, event)
        self.seq = 0
        self.arrivals = []         # [(at, payload)] sorted, consumed by whoever advances past them
        self.inject = None         # payload -> None; runs with the clock held still
        self.advances = 0
        self.parked = []           # every real Event a parked thread is blocked on, so a deadlock can wake them all
        self.dead = None

    def sleep(self, secs):
        """Park the calling thread until now + secs."""
        ev = threading.Event()
        with self.lock:
            self.seq += 1
            heapq.heappush(self.sleepers, (self.now + max(0, int(secs)), self.seq, ev))
        self.park(ev)

    def park(self, ev):
        with self.lock:
            self.parked.append(ev)
            self.running -= 1
            self._advance_if_idle()
        ev.wait()
        with self.lock:
            if ev in self.parked:
                self.parked.remove(ev)
        if self.dead:
            raise Deadlock(self.dead)

    def _advance_if_idle(self):
        while self.running == 0 and not self.dead:
            nxt_arr = self.arrivals[0][0] if self.arrivals else None
            nxt_slp = self.sleepers[0][0] if self.sleepers else None
            if nxt_arr is None and nxt_slp is None:
                self.dead = "every thread is parked and nothing is due: the candidate is waiting on something it never signals"
                for e in self.parked:
                    e.set()
                return
            if nxt_arr is not None and (nxt_slp is None or nxt_arr <= nxt_slp):
                self.now = max(self.now, nxt_arr)
                _, payload = self.arrivals.pop(0)
                self.running += 1
                self.lock.release()
                try:
                    self.inject(payload)
                finally:
                    self.lock.acquire()
                    self.running -= 1
                continue
            self.now = max(self.now, nxt_slp)
            self.advances += 1
            while self.sleepers and self.sleepers[0][0] <= self.now:
                _, _, e = heapq.heappop(self.sleepers)
                self.running += 1
                e.set()


class FakeThreading:
    """The `threading` the candidate sees: Thread/Event/Condition report to the Clock; everything else is real."""

    def __init__(self, clock):
        self.clock = clock
        real = threading
        self.Lock, self.RLock, self.local = real.Lock, real.RLock, real.local
        self.current_thread, self.main_thread = real.current_thread, real.main_thread
        self.get_ident = real.get_ident
        clk = clock

        class Thread:
            def __init__(self, group=None, target=None, name=None, args=(), kwargs=None, daemon=None):
                self._target, self._args, self._kwargs, self.name = target, args, kwargs or {}, name
                self._joiners, self._finished, self._t = [], False, None

            def start(self):
                with clk.lock:
                    clk.running += 1
                self._t = real.Thread(target=self._run, name=self.name, daemon=True)
                self._t.start()

            def _run(self):
                try:
                    if self._target:
                        self._target(*self._args, **self._kwargs)
                except Deadlock:
                    pass
                finally:
                    with clk.lock:
                        self._finished = True
                        for e in self._joiners:
                            clk.running += 1
                            e.set()
                        self._joiners = []
                        clk.running -= 1
                        clk._advance_if_idle()

            def join(self, timeout=None):
                with clk.lock:
                    if self._finished:
                        return
                    e = real.Event()
                    self._joiners.append(e)
                clk.park(e)

            def is_alive(self):
                return self._t is not None and not self._finished

        class Event:
            def __init__(self):
                self._set, self._waiters = False, []

            def is_set(self):
                return self._set

            def set(self):
                with clk.lock:
                    self._set = True
                    ws, self._waiters = self._waiters, []
                    for e in ws:
                        clk.running += 1
                        e.set()

            def clear(self):
                self._set = False

            def wait(self, timeout=None):
                with clk.lock:
                    if self._set:
                        return True
                    e = real.Event()
                    self._waiters.append(e)
                clk.park(e)
                return True

        class Condition:
            def __init__(self, lock=None):
                self._lock, self._waiters = lock or real.RLock(), []

            def __enter__(self):
                self._lock.acquire()
                return self

            def __exit__(self, *a):
                self._lock.release()
                return False

            acquire = lambda self, *a, **k: self._lock.acquire(*a, **k)
            release = lambda self: self._lock.release()

            def wait(self, timeout=None):
                with clk.lock:
                    e = real.Event()
                    self._waiters.append(e)
                self._lock.release()
                try:
                    clk.park(e)
                finally:
                    self._lock.acquire()
                return True

            def notify_all(self):
                with clk.lock:
                    ws, self._waiters = self._waiters, []
                    for e in ws:
                        clk.running += 1
                        e.set()

            notify = notify_all

        self.Thread, self.Event, self.Condition = Thread, Event, Condition


class FakeTime:
    def __init__(self, clock):
        self._c = clock

    def time(self):
        return float(self._c.now)

    def gmtime(self, secs=None):
        return time.gmtime(self._c.now if secs is None else secs)

    def sleep(self, secs):
        self._c.sleep(secs)

    def __getattr__(self, name):
        return getattr(time, name)


class FakeOsPath:
    def __init__(self, mtimes, clock):
        self._m, self._c = mtimes, clock

    def getmtime(self, path):
        return float(self._m.get(path, self._c.now))

    def __getattr__(self, name):
        return getattr(os.path, name)


class FakeOs:
    """`os` with two answers of the harness's: getmtime from the table write_atomic fills (durable time is a
    stamp, never the disk's clock) and access(X_OK) answering which gates a checkout has without one existing."""

    def __init__(self, world, mtimes, clock):
        self._w = world
        self.path = FakeOsPath(mtimes, clock)

    def access(self, path, mode, **kw):
        rel = self._w.gate_rel(path)
        if rel is not None:
            return rel in self._w.gates_of(self._w.repo_of_path(path))
        return os.access(path, mode, **kw)

    def __getattr__(self, name):
        return getattr(os, name)


# ── the world: what the trace says happened, answered to whoever asks ────────────────────────────────────
class World:
    def __init__(self, trace, root, clock, conflicts="files", log=None):
        self.trace, self.root, self.clock, self.conflicts = trace, root, clock, conflicts
        self.log = log or (lambda s: None)
        self.prs = {(l["repo"], l["pr"]): l for l in trace["landings"]}
        self.repos = trace.get("repos") or {}
        self.med = trace["medians"]
        self.state = {}         # (repo, pr) -> live state
        self.merges = []        # [(seq, repo, pr, at, files)]
        self.tip = {}           # repo -> synthetic default-branch sha
        self.digest, self.mark, self.v2_markers = change_digest, "cc-land-review", True   # the candidate's own, once loaded
        self.mtimes = {}
        self.rearm, self.work_wanted = [], False
        self.n = {"suites": 0, "gates": 0, "reviews": 0, "repairs": 0, "merges": 0, "conflicts": 0,
                  "behind": 0, "updates": 0, "person": 0}
        self.calls = []
        # v2 only, so a v1 trace scores to the bytes it always did: git plumbing answered from CONTENT SETS. A commit
        # holds a set of changes ("pr:gen"); the base tip holds every change merged so far, a head the changes merged
        # before its base plus its own, a merge the union; a tree is named by its set. So merge_result builds the
        # merge a real checkout would, and the candidate's own reads of it — mergeability, how far behind a head
        # stands, the tree a merge would leave — are answered as a checkout would have answered them.
        self.v2 = trace.get("version", 1) >= 2
        self.changes = []       # [(repo, "pr:gen")], in step with self.merges
        self.commits, self.trees = {}, {}
        for key, l in self.prs.items():
            self.state[key] = {"merged_at": None, "comments": [], "base_seq": 0, "fix": None, "fix_gens": 0,
                               "fix_pushes": [], "extra_gens": 0, "updates": []}

    # -- where a path points --
    def repo_of_path(self, path):
        m = re.search(r"/cc-land\.\w+\.([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)\.(\d+|base)\.[^/]+(?:/|$)", path or "")
        if m:
            return m.group(1)
        m = re.match(re.escape(self.root) + r"/dev/([^/]+)", path or "")
        return m.group(1) if m else ""

    def pr_of_path(self, path):
        m = re.search(r"/cc-land\.\w+\.([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)\.(\d+)\.[^/]+(?:/|$)", path or "")
        return (m.group(1), int(m.group(2))) if m else None

    def gate_rel(self, path):
        m = re.search(r"/cc-land\.\w+\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.(?:\d+|base)\.[^/]+/head/(.+)$", path or "")
        if m:
            return m.group(1)
        m = re.match(re.escape(self.root) + r"/dev/[^/]+/(.+)$", path or "")
        return m.group(1) if m else None

    def gates_of(self, repo):
        return (self.repos.get(repo) or {}).get("gates") or []

    def base_of(self, repo):
        return (self.repos.get(repo) or {}).get("default_branch") or "main"

    def board(self, repo):
        tracks = {}
        for (r, pr), l in sorted(self.prs.items()):
            if r == repo and (l.get("branch") or "").startswith("track/"):
                tracks[l["branch"][6:]] = {"pr": f"https://example.invalid/o/r/pull/{pr}", "branch": l["branch"],
                                           "status": "merged" if self.state[(r, pr)]["merged_at"] else "review"}
        return {"default_branch": self.base_of(repo), "path": f"{self.root}/dev/{repo}", "tracks": tracks}

    # -- the head, over time --
    def head(self, key, at=None):
        l, st, at = self.prs[key], self.state[key], self.clock.now if at is None else at
        cur = l["heads"][0]
        cur_at = epoch(cur["at"])
        for h in l["heads"]:
            if h["via"] == "fix":
                continue
            if epoch(h["at"]) <= at and h["gen"] >= cur["gen"]:
                cur, cur_at = h, epoch(h["at"])
        fix_heads = [h for h in l["heads"] if h["via"] == "fix"]
        for i, pushed_at in enumerate(st["fix_pushes"]):
            if pushed_at <= at:
                h = fix_heads[i] if i < len(fix_heads) else {"sha": hexname(key, "fix", i), "gen": (fix_heads[-1]["gen"] if fix_heads else cur["gen"]) + 1 + (i - len(fix_heads))}
                if h["gen"] >= cur["gen"]:
                    cur, cur_at = h, pushed_at
        for u_at, sha, gen in st["updates"]:      # the base merged in (v2): the same change on a new head
            if u_at <= at and gen >= cur["gen"] and u_at >= cur_at:
                cur, cur_at = {"sha": sha, "gen": gen}, u_at
        return cur["sha"], cur["gen"]

    def verdict_for(self, key, sha, gen):
        l = self.prs[key]
        for v in l["verdicts"]:
            if v["head"] == sha[:12] and v["kind"] == "bought":
                return v["verdict"], v.get("cost") or 0
        for v in l["verdicts"]:
            if v.get("gen") == gen:
                return v["verdict"], v.get("cost") or 0
        if l.get("merged"):     # the PR's eventual verdict: it landed, so the last diff anyone read was a LAND
            return "LAND", 0
        if l["verdicts"]:
            return l["verdicts"][-1]["verdict"], l["verdicts"][-1].get("cost") or 0
        return "LAND", 0

    def record(self, key, v):
        """A verdict a PERSON wrote down (`cc-land record`), put on the PR at the time they did, in the shape the
        candidate itself writes — keyed by the change where it keys by the change, by the head where it does not —
        so the candidate reads it as its own and does not buy the same answer again."""
        l, st = self.prs[key], self.state[key]
        h = next((h for h in l["heads"] if h["sha"][:12] == (v.get("head") or "")[:12]), None)
        sha, gen = (h["sha"], h["gen"]) if h else self.head(key)
        by = re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._@-]+", "-", v.get("by") or "a-person")
        if self.v2_markers:
            body = (f"<!-- {self.mark} v2 change={self.digest(self.synth_diff(key, gen))} base={self.mb(key)[:12]} "
                    f"head={sha[:12]} verdict={v['verdict']} by={by} -->")
        else:
            body = f"<!-- {self.mark} {sha[:12]} {v['verdict']} -->"
        st["comments"].append({"body": f"{body}\n{v['verdict']} — recorded by {by}, replayed from history",
                               "viewerDidAuthor": True, "createdAt": stamp(self.clock.now)})
        self.log(f"{stamp(self.clock.now)} recorded {key} {v['verdict']} by {by} at {sha[:12]}")
        # A recorded LAND is a person saying "land this": in history the job was either still waiting in a slow
        # queue or they queued it again a second later. A faster candidate may have finished the job before the
        # record came, and nobody in a replay types the re-queue — so the record does, when the PR is still open.
        return v["verdict"] == "LAND" and st["merged_at"] is None

    def conflicting(self, key):
        """The brief's rule: "a PR conflicts when a PR merged since its base IN THE REPLAY'S ORDER touches one of
        its files" — under `files` for every PR, under `history` only for a PR history saw conflict."""
        if self.conflicts == "none" or (self.conflicts == "history" and not self.prs[key].get("conflicted")):
            return False
        st, mine = self.state[key], {p for _, p in self.prs[key]["files"]}
        for seq, repo, pr, at, files in self.merges:
            if repo == key[0] and seq >= st["base_seq"] and (repo, pr) != key and mine & files:
                return True
        return False

    def rebase(self, key):
        self.state[key]["base_seq"] = len(self.merges)

    def behind(self, key):
        """How many merges into its repo the PR's base has not seen, in the replay's order."""
        st = self.state[key]
        return sum(1 for seq, repo, pr, _, _ in self.merges if repo == key[0] and seq >= st["base_seq"] and (repo, pr) != key)

    def refused_behind(self, key):
        """v2: GitHub refuses the merge of a PR history saw stopped merely behind, whenever the replay has it behind
        at all — the rule it enforces is binary. Only those PRs, like --conflicts history: a queue that merges behind
        branches every day says GitHub does not refuse every one. The distance history recorded is calibration only."""
        return self.v2 and any(s.get("kind") == "behind" for s in self.prs[key].get("stops") or []) and self.behind(key) > 0

    def land(self, key, why="merged"):
        repo, pr = key
        _, gen = self.head(key)
        self.state[key]["merged_at"] = self.clock.now
        self.merges.append((len(self.merges), repo, pr, self.clock.now, {p for _, p in self.prs[key]["files"]}))
        self.changes.append((repo, f"{pr}:{gen}"))
        self.tip[repo] = hexname(repo, "tip", len(self.merges))
        self.commits[self.tip[repo]] = frozenset(c for r, c in self.changes if r == repo)
        self.n["merges"] += 1
        self.log(f"{stamp(self.clock.now)} {why} {repo}#{pr}")

    def person_merge(self, key):
        """v2: a PR a person merged by hand in history is merged at that time here too. The brief: "a hand merge
        stays the person's action at its time unless the candidate's own logic lands the PR earlier"."""
        if self.state[key]["merged_at"] is not None:     # the candidate landed it earlier: not the person's
            return
        self.n["person"] += 1
        self.land(key, "a person merged")

    def content(self, repo, sha):
        """The set of changes a commit holds (v2), or None for a commit nobody made."""
        sha = (sha or "").strip()
        if sha in ("HEAD", self.base_of(repo), f"origin/{self.base_of(repo)}"):
            sha = self.tip.get(repo) or hexname(repo, "tip", 0)
        if sha in self.commits:
            return self.commits[sha]
        if sha == hexname(repo, "tip", 0):
            return frozenset()
        key = self.key_of_sha(repo, sha) if sha else None
        if not key:
            return None
        st = self.state[key]
        gens = [(h["sha"], h["gen"]) for h in self.prs[key]["heads"]] + [(s, g) for _, s, g in st["updates"]]
        gen = next((g for s, g in gens if sha.startswith(s) or s.startswith(sha[:12])), None)
        if gen is None:
            gen = self.head(key)[1]
        return frozenset([c for r, c in self.changes[:st["base_seq"]] if r == repo] + [f"{key[1]}:{gen}"])

    def plumbing(self, repo, sub, args):
        """v2: what merge_result asks — rev-parse X^{commit}, merge-base --is-ancestor, merge-tree, commit-tree —
        and rev-list --count A..B, answered from content sets. None for anything else."""
        revs = [a for a in args if not a.startswith("-")]
        if sub == "rev-parse" and revs and revs[-1].endswith("^{commit}"):
            what = revs[-1][:-len("^{commit}")]
            if self.content(repo, what) is None:
                return 1, ""
            sha = (self.tip.get(repo) or hexname(repo, "tip", 0)) if what in ("HEAD", f"origin/{self.base_of(repo)}") else what
            return 0, sha + "0" * max(0, 40 - len(sha)) + "\n"
        if sub == "merge-base" and "--is-ancestor" in args and len(revs) >= 2:
            a, b = self.content(repo, revs[-2]), self.content(repo, revs[-1])
            return (128, "fatal: not a commit") if a is None or b is None else (0 if a <= b else 1, "")
        if sub == "merge-tree" and len(revs) >= 2:
            a, b = self.content(repo, revs[-2]), self.content(repo, revs[-1])
            if a is None or b is None:
                return 128, "fatal: not a commit"
            tree = hexname("tree", *sorted(a | b))
            self.trees[tree] = a | b
            return 0, tree + "\n"
        if sub == "commit-tree" and args and args[0] in self.trees:
            sha = hexname("commit", args[0], *[args[i + 1] for i, a in enumerate(args[:-1]) if a == "-p"])
            self.commits[sha] = self.trees[args[0]]
            return 0, sha + "\n"
        if sub == "rev-list" and "--count" in args and revs and ".." in revs[-1]:
            a, b = (self.content(repo, x) for x in revs[-1].split("..", 1))
            return 0, f"{len(b - a) if a is not None and b is not None else 0}\n"
        return None

    # -- the answers --
    def gh(self, argv, cwd):
        repo = self.repo_of_path(cwd)
        if len(argv) < 4 or argv[1] != "pr" or not repo:
            return 1, "gh: not answered here"
        try:
            pr = int(argv[3])
        except ValueError:
            return 1, "gh: bad pr"
        key = (repo, pr)
        if key not in self.prs:
            return 1, f"no pull requests found for #{pr}"
        l, st = self.prs[key], self.state[key]
        if argv[2] == "view":
            fields = argv[argv.index("--json") + 1].split(",") if "--json" in argv else []
            sha, gen = self.head(key)
            merged = st["merged_at"] is not None
            facts = {"number": pr, "title": l.get("title") or f"PR #{pr}", "url": f"https://example.invalid/o/r/pull/{pr}",
                     "state": "MERGED" if merged else "OPEN",
                     "mergeable": "CONFLICTING" if (not merged and self.conflicting(key)) else "MERGEABLE",
                     "headRefName": l.get("branch") or f"pr-{pr}", "headRefOid": sha + "0" * (40 - len(sha)),
                     "mergeCommit": {"oid": hexname(key, "merge")} if merged else None,
                     "mergedAt": stamp(st["merged_at"]) if merged else None,
                     "comments": [dict(c) for c in st["comments"]]}
            if self.v2:
                facts["mergeStateStatus"] = ("MERGED" if merged else "DIRTY" if facts["mergeable"] == "CONFLICTING"
                                             else "BEHIND" if self.behind(key) else "CLEAN")
            return 0, json.dumps({k: facts.get(k) for k in fields} if fields else facts)
        if argv[2] == "update-branch" and self.v2:
            # GitHub's Update branch button: the base merged into the branch, a new head holding the same change.
            if st["merged_at"] is not None or self.conflicting(key):
                return 1, "X Cannot update PR branch due to conflicts" if st["merged_at"] is None else "X PR is merged"
            if not self.behind(key):
                return 0, "! PR branch already up-to-date\n"
            self.clock.sleep(UPDATE_SECS)
            _, gen = self.head(key)
            sha = hexname(key, "update", len(st["updates"]))[:12]
            self.rebase(key)
            st["updates"].append((self.clock.now, sha, gen))
            self.n["updates"] += 1
            self.log(f"{stamp(self.clock.now)} updated {repo}#{pr} with its base: head {sha}")
            return 0, "✓ PR branch updated\n"
        if argv[2] == "comment":
            body = argv[argv.index("--body") + 1] if "--body" in argv else ""
            st["comments"].append({"body": body, "viewerDidAuthor": True, "createdAt": stamp(self.clock.now)})
            return 0, f"https://example.invalid/o/r/pull/{pr}#issuecomment-{len(st['comments'])}"
        if argv[2] == "merge":
            if st["merged_at"] is not None:
                return 1, "GraphQL: Pull request already merged"
            sha, gen = self.head(key)
            want = argv[argv.index("--match-head-commit") + 1] if "--match-head-commit" in argv else ""
            if want and not want.startswith(sha):
                return 1, "GraphQL: Head branch was modified. Review and try the merge again."
            if self.conflicting(key):
                self.n["conflicts"] += 1
                return 1, "GraphQL: Pull Request has merge conflicts (mergePullRequest)"
            if self.refused_behind(key):
                self.n["behind"] += 1
                self.log(f"{stamp(self.clock.now)} refused {repo}#{pr}: {self.behind(key)} merge(s) behind")
                return 1, (f"X Pull request #{pr} is not mergeable: the base branch policy prohibits the merge.\n"
                           "To have the pull request merged after all the requirements have been met, add the `--auto` flag.")
            self.land(key)
            return 0, ""
        return 1, "gh: not answered here"

    def git(self, argv, cwd, stdout_only=False):
        repo, key = self.repo_of_path(cwd), self.pr_of_path(cwd)
        sub = argv[1] if len(argv) > 1 else ""
        args = argv[2:]
        base = self.base_of(repo)
        tip = self.tip.get(repo) or hexname(repo, "tip", 0)
        if sub in ("fetch", "pull", "worktree"):
            return 0, ""
        answered = self.plumbing(repo, sub, args) if self.v2 else None
        if answered is not None:
            return answered
        if sub == "ls-remote":
            out = []
            for ref in args[1:]:
                m = re.match(r"refs/pull/(\d+)/head", ref)
                pr = int(m.group(1)) if m else next((p for (r, p), l in self.prs.items() if r == repo and f"refs/heads/{l.get('branch')}" == ref), None)
                if pr is not None and (repo, pr) in self.prs:
                    sha, _ = self.head((repo, pr))
                    out.append(f"{sha + '0' * (40 - len(sha))}\t{ref}")
            return 0, "\n".join(out) + ("\n" if out else "")
        if sub == "rev-parse":
            what = args[-1] if args else ""
            if what == "FETCH_HEAD":
                key = self._fetched.get(repo)
                if not key:
                    return 128, "fatal: no FETCH_HEAD"
                sha, _ = self.head(key)
                return 0, sha + "0" * (40 - len(sha)) + "\n"
            if what == "--abbrev-ref" or "--abbrev-ref" in args:
                return 0, base + "\n"
            if what == "HEAD^{tree}":
                if key and key in self.prs:
                    sha, gen = self.head(key)
                    if any(s == sha for _, s, _ in self.state[key]["updates"]):
                        return 0, hexname(key, "tree", gen, sha) + "\n"    # a tree no recorded green run was on
                    return 0, self.tree_id(key, gen) + "\n"
                return 0, hexname(repo, "basetree", tip) + "\n"
            if what in ("HEAD", f"origin/{base}"):
                return 0, tip + "\n"
            return 0, hexname(what) + "\n"
        if sub == "merge-base":
            pr_key = self.key_of_sha(repo, args[-1])
            return (0, self.mb(pr_key) + "\n") if pr_key else (128, "fatal: no merge base")
        if sub == "rev-list":
            return 0, "0\n"
        if sub == "remote":
            return 0, "git@example.invalid:o/r.git\n"
        if sub == "show":
            spec = args[-1] if args else ""
            if "--name-status" in args:
                pr_key = self.key_of_merge(spec)
                return (0, self.name_status(pr_key)) if pr_key else (0, "")
            path = spec.split(":", 1)[1] if ":" in spec else ""
            ctl = (self.repos.get(repo) or {}).get("control")
            if ctl and path == ctl[0]:
                return 0, ctl[1]
            return 128, f"fatal: path '{path}' does not exist"
        if sub == "diff":
            flags = [a for a in args if a.startswith("-")]
            revs = [a for a in args if not a.startswith("-")]
            pr_key = next((self.key_of_sha(repo, r) for r in reversed(revs) if self.key_of_sha(repo, r)), None)
            if not pr_key:
                return 0, ""
            l = self.prs[pr_key]
            if "--name-status" in flags:
                return 0, self.name_status(pr_key)
            if "--numstat" in flags:
                return 0, "".join(f"{a}\t{d}\t{p}\n" for p, (a, d) in sorted(l["perfile"].items())) or \
                    "".join(f"{l.get('adds', 1)}\t{l.get('dels', 0)}\t{p}\n" for _, p in l["files"])
            if "--name-only" in flags:
                return 0, ""
            if "-U0" in flags:
                return 1, ""
            _, gen = self.head(pr_key)
            return 0, self.synth_diff(pr_key, gen)
        return 0, ""

    _fetched = {}

    def note_fetch(self, repo, spec):
        m = re.match(r"(?:refs/heads/(.+)|pull/(\d+)/head)$", spec or "")
        if not m:
            return
        if m.group(2):
            self._fetched[repo] = (repo, int(m.group(2)))
        else:
            for (r, p), l in self.prs.items():
                if r == repo and l.get("branch") == m.group(1):
                    self._fetched[repo] = (r, p)

    def key_of_sha(self, repo, sha):
        for (r, p), l in self.prs.items():
            if r != repo:
                continue
            for h in l["heads"]:
                if sha.startswith(h["sha"]) or h["sha"].startswith(sha[:12]):
                    return (r, p)
            for i in range(self.state[(r, p)]["fix_pushes"].__len__()):
                if sha.startswith(hexname((r, p), "fix", i)):
                    return (r, p)
            for _, u, _ in self.state[(r, p)]["updates"]:
                if sha.startswith(u):
                    return (r, p)
        return None

    def key_of_merge(self, sha):
        for key in self.prs:
            if sha.startswith(hexname(key, "merge")):
                return key
        return None

    def mb(self, key):
        return hexname(key, "base")

    def tree_id(self, key, gen):
        return hexname(key, "tree", gen)

    def name_status(self, key):
        return "".join(f"{s}\t{p}\n" for s, p in self.prs[key]["files"])

    def synth_diff(self, key, gen):
        out = []
        for s, p in self.prs[key]["files"]:
            out.append(f"diff --git a/{p} b/{p}\nindex 0000000..1111111 100644\n--- a/{p}\n+++ b/{p}\n@@ -1 +1 @@\n"
                       f"-{key[0]}#{key[1]} before\n+{key[0]}#{key[1]} change {gen} of {p}\n")
        return "".join(out)

    def gate(self, argv, cwd):
        key = self.pr_of_path(cwd)
        rel = self.gate_rel(argv[0]) or os.path.basename(argv[0])
        g = os.path.basename(rel)
        self.n["gates"] += 1
        if rel in SUITE:
            self.n["suites"] += 1
        secs = self.med["gate"].get(g, 300)
        red = False
        if key and key in self.prs:
            l = self.prs[key]
            secs = l["gates"].get(g) or secs
            sha, _ = self.head(key)
            red = sha[:12] in (l["red"].get(g) or [])
        self.log(f"{stamp(self.clock.now)} gate {g} for {key} {secs}s {'RED' if red else 'green'}")
        self.clock.sleep(secs)
        return (1, "  ✗ a case history saw fail\n1 failed\n") if red else (0, "  ✓ every one\n0 failed\n")

    def review(self, argv, cwd):
        prompt = argv[2] if len(argv) > 2 else ""
        m = re.search(r"cc-replay:(\S+):(\d+)", prompt)
        key = (m.group(1), int(m.group(2))) if m else self.pr_of_path(cwd)
        self.n["reviews"] += 1
        secs, verdict, cost = self.med["review"], "LAND", 0.0
        if key in self.prs:
            l = self.prs[key]
            secs = median(l["review_secs"], secs)
            sha, gen = self.head(key)
            verdict, cost = self.verdict_for(key, sha, gen)
        self.log(f"{stamp(self.clock.now)} review {key} {int(secs)}s -> {verdict}")
        self.clock.sleep(secs)
        obj = {"verdict": verdict, "findings": [] if verdict == "LAND" else
               [{"where": "somewhere", "what": "what history's reviewer found", "fix": "what it asked for"}]}
        return 0, json.dumps({"result": json.dumps(obj), "structured_output": obj, "total_cost_usd": cost or 1.0,
                              "usage": {"input_tokens": 1000, "output_tokens": 100}, "num_turns": 5})

    def fix(self, argv):
        repo, track = argv[1], argv[2]
        key = next(((r, p) for (r, p), l in self.prs.items() if r == repo and l.get("branch") == f"track/{track}"), None)
        self.n["repairs"] += 1
        if key:
            st, l = self.state[key], self.prs[key]
            i = len(st["fix_pushes"])
            latency = (epoch(l["fixes"][i]["pushed"]) - epoch(l["fixes"][i]["dispatched"])) if i < len(l["fixes"]) and l["fixes"][i].get("pushed") else 0
            latency = latency if latency > 0 else self.med["fix"]
            st["fix_pushes"].append(self.clock.now + latency)
            st["fix"] = (self.clock.now, self.clock.now + latency)
            self.log(f"{stamp(self.clock.now)} repair {key} pushes in {latency}s")
        return 0, ""

    def track_status(self, repo, track):
        key = next(((r, p) for (r, p), l in self.prs.items() if r == repo and l.get("branch") == f"track/{track}"), None)
        if key and self.state[key]["fix"] and self.state[key]["fix"][1] > self.clock.now:
            return "running"
        return "merged" if key and self.state[key]["merged_at"] is not None else "review"

    def sh(self, argv, cwd=None, timeout=300, stdout_only=False, **kw):
        tool = os.path.basename(argv[0]) if argv else ""
        self.calls.append(tool)
        if tool == "git":
            if len(argv) > 3 and argv[1] == "fetch":
                self.note_fetch(self.repo_of_path(cwd), argv[-1])
            return self.git(argv, cwd, stdout_only)
        if tool == "gh":
            return self.gh(argv, cwd)
        if tool == "claude":
            return self.review(argv, cwd)
        if tool == "systemd-run":
            on = next((a for a in argv if a.startswith("--on-active=")), "")
            if on:
                self.rearm.append(int(on.split("=", 1)[1]))
            else:
                self.work_wanted = True
            return 0, ""
        if tool == "systemctl":
            return (0, "inactive\n") if "is-active" in argv else (0, "disabled\n") if "is-enabled" in argv else (0, "")
        if tool == "cc-board":
            if len(argv) > 4 and argv[1] == "get" and argv[4] == "status":
                return 0, self.track_status(argv[2], argv[3]) + "\n"
            return 0, ""
        if tool == "cc-limit":
            return 1, "clear\n"
        if tool == "cc-scope":
            return 1, "no ledger\n"
        if tool == "cc":
            if "--go" in argv:
                return self.fix(argv)
            return 0, ""
        if tool in ("tmux", "pgrep", "cc-pause"):
            return 1, ""
        return 0, ""


# ── the harness: import the candidate, rebind its seams, drive the trace through it ──────────────────────
NOT_MONOLITH = ("not the old single-file landing tool, the only kind this harness holds; the lander that "
                "replaced it is a package, and scoring it is retired with cc-improve (docs/improve-loop.md)")


def load_candidate(path, root, world, clock, verbose_log):
    binq = f"{root}/bin"
    os.makedirs(binq, exist_ok=True)
    os.makedirs(f"{root}/config", exist_ok=True)
    dst = f"{binq}/cc-land"
    shutil.copyfile(path, dst)
    with open(f"{root}/config/review-prompt.md", "w") as f:
        f.write("cc-replay:@REPO@:@PR@ review of @TITLE@ at @TREE@ diff @DIFF@ brief @BRIEF@ rules @RULES@\n")
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("cc_land_candidate", importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("cc_land_candidate", dst))
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)
    ns = mod.__dict__
    for k in ("sh", "run_gate", "cmd_work", "cmd_queue", "write_atomic", "stamp", "LANDQ", "STATE", "BOARDS"):
        if k not in ns:
            raise SystemExit(f"cc-replay: {path} has no `{k}` — {NOT_MONOLITH}")
    real_write = ns["write_atomic"]
    world.digest = ns.get("change_digest") or change_digest
    world.mark = ns.get("REVIEW_MARK") or "cc-land-review"
    world.v2_markers = "by" in inspect.signature(ns["Land"].marker).parameters if "Land" in ns else False

    def write_atomic(p, obj):
        real_write(p, obj)
        world.mtimes[p] = clock.now

    ns.update(threading=FakeThreading(clock), time=FakeTime(clock), os=FakeOs(world, world.mtimes, clock),
              sh=world.sh, run_gate=lambda argv, cwd, log, env, stop=None: world.gate(argv, cwd), write_atomic=write_atomic,
              board=world.board, repo_root=lambda r: f"{root}/dev/{r}", paused=lambda t: False,
              linked_units=lambda: [], read_unit=lambda u: "")
    if "default_signals" in ns:
        ns["default_signals"] = lambda: None
    return mod


def score(candidate, trace, conflicts="history", verbose=False, keep_root=False):
    root = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-replay-")
    saved_env = {k: os.environ.get(k) for k in ("HOME", "CC_CLAUDE", "CC_GREEN_DIR", "TMPDIR")}
    saved_tmp = tempfile.tempdir
    chatter = io.StringIO()
    logl = []
    log = (lambda s: logl.append(s)) if verbose else (lambda s: None)
    try:
        os.makedirs(f"{root}/tmp")
        os.environ.update(HOME=root, CC_CLAUDE=f"{root}/bin/claude", TMPDIR=f"{root}/tmp")
        os.environ.pop("CC_GREEN_DIR", None)
        tempfile.tempdir = f"{root}/tmp"
        arrivals = [(epoch(a["at"]), 1, l["repo"], l["pr"], None) for l in trace["landings"] for a in l["arrivals"] if epoch(a["at"])]
        if not arrivals:
            raise SystemExit("cc-replay: the trace has no arrivals")
        records = [(epoch(v["at"]), 0, l["repo"], l["pr"], v) for l in trace["landings"] for v in l["verdicts"]
                   if v.get("kind") == "recorded" and epoch(v["at"])]
        persons = [(epoch(l["person"]["at"]), 2, l["repo"], l["pr"], None) for l in trace["landings"]
                   if trace.get("version", 1) >= 2 and l.get("person") and epoch(l["person"].get("at"))]
        events = sorted(arrivals + records + persons, key=lambda e: e[:4])    # one second: the record, the queue, the hand merge
        clock = Clock(events[0][0] - 1)
        world = World(trace, root, clock, conflicts, log)
        for repo in sorted({l["repo"] for l in trace["landings"]}):
            os.makedirs(f"{root}/dev/{repo}/.git", exist_ok=True)
            for l in trace["landings"]:
                if l["repo"] == repo and (l.get("branch") or "").startswith("track/"):
                    os.makedirs(f"{root}/.cc/state/{repo}/{l['branch'][6:]}", exist_ok=True)
        landq = f"{root}/.cc/state/land"
        os.makedirs(f"{landq}/green", exist_ok=True)
        for l in trace["landings"]:        # the green records history spent, for the head they were spent on
            key = (l["repo"], l["pr"])
            for g in l.get("green") or []:
                gate = next((x for x in world.gates_of(l["repo"]) if os.path.basename(x) == g), g)
                for h in l["heads"]:
                    tree = world.tree_id(key, h["gen"])
                    with open(f"{landq}/green/{g}-{tree[:12]}.json", "w") as f:
                        json.dump({"suite": gate, "tree": tree, "scope": "", "at": l["arrivals"][0]["at"] if l["arrivals"] else stamp(clock.now)}, f)
        mod = load_candidate(candidate, root, world, clock, log)

        def inject(payload):
            kind, repo, pr, v = payload
            if kind == 2:
                world.person_merge((repo, pr))
                return
            if kind == 0 and not world.record((repo, pr), v):
                return
            world.rebase((repo, pr))
            with contextlib_redirect(chatter):
                mod.cmd_queue([repo, str(pr), "--who", "replay"])
            log(f"{stamp(clock.now)} queued {repo}#{pr}{' after the recorded LAND' if kind == 0 else ''}")

        clock.inject = inject
        clock.arrivals = [(e[0], e[1:]) for e in events]
        armed, sweeps = [], 0
        while True:
            nxt_arr = clock.arrivals[0][0] if clock.arrivals else None
            nxt_arm = min(armed) if armed else None
            if nxt_arr is None and nxt_arm is None:
                break
            t = min(x for x in (nxt_arr, nxt_arm) if x is not None)
            clock.now = max(clock.now, t)
            world.work_wanted = False
            while clock.arrivals and clock.arrivals[0][0] <= clock.now:
                _, payload = clock.arrivals.pop(0)
                inject(payload)
            due = [a for a in armed if a <= clock.now]
            if not due and not world.work_wanted:
                continue
            armed = [a for a in armed if a > clock.now]
            world.rearm = []
            sweeps += 1
            log(f"{stamp(clock.now)} sweep {sweeps}")
            with contextlib_redirect(chatter):
                mod.cmd_work([])
            if clock.dead:
                raise Deadlock(clock.dead)
            armed += [clock.now + s for s in world.rearm]
            if sweeps > 100000:
                raise SystemExit("cc-replay: runaway sweep loop")
        return report(trace, world, clock, sweeps), "\n".join(logl), chatter.getvalue()
    finally:
        for k, v in saved_env.items():
            if v is None:
                os.environ.pop(k, None)
            else:
                os.environ[k] = v
        tempfile.tempdir = saved_tmp
        if not keep_root:
            shutil.rmtree(root, ignore_errors=True)


class contextlib_redirect:
    def __init__(self, buf):
        self.buf = buf

    def __enter__(self):
        self.o, self.e = sys.stdout, sys.stderr
        sys.stdout = sys.stderr = self.buf

    def __exit__(self, *a):
        sys.stdout, sys.stderr = self.o, self.e
        return False


def report(trace, world, clock, sweeps):
    rows, mins, both, both_q = [], [], [], []
    for l in sorted(trace["landings"], key=lambda l: (l["repo"], l["pr"])):
        key = (l["repo"], l["pr"])
        first = min((epoch(a["at"]) for a in l["arrivals"] if epoch(a["at"])), default=0)
        st = world.state[key]
        m_rep = st["merged_at"]
        hist = epoch(l.get("merged") or "")
        rmin = (m_rep - first) / 60 if m_rep is not None and first else None
        hmin = (hist - first) / 60 if hist and first else None
        if rmin is not None:
            mins.append(rmin)
        via = "queue" if l.get("queue_merged") else ("hand" if hist else "-")
        if rmin is not None and hmin is not None:
            both.append(hmin)
            if via == "queue":
                both_q.append(hmin)
        rows.append((f"{l['repo']}#{l['pr']}", stamp(first)[:16] if first else "-", stamp(m_rep)[:16] if m_rep is not None else "-",
                     f"{rmin:.1f}" if rmin is not None else "-", stamp(hist)[:16] if hist else "-", f"{hmin:.1f}" if hmin is not None else "-", via))
    n = world.n
    total = len(trace["landings"])
    merged = sum(1 for r in rows if r[2] != "-")
    med = statistics.median(mins) if mins else 0.0
    lines = [f"score {med:.1f} suites={n['suites']} reviews={n['reviews']} repairs={n['repairs']} unmerged={total - merged} merged={merged}/{total}",
             f"gates={n['gates']} conflicts={n['conflicts']} sweeps={sweeps} clock-advances={clock.advances} "
             f"span={stamp(clock.now)[:16]} hand-merged={sum(1 for r in rows if r[6] == 'hand')}"
             + (f" trace=v2 behind-refused={n['behind']} base-updates={n['updates']} "
                f"person-merged={n['person']}" if world.v2 else ""),
             f"history {statistics.median(both) if both else 0.0:.1f} over the {len(both)} PRs both merged "
             f"({statistics.median(both_q) if both_q else 0.0:.1f} over the {len(both_q)} the queue merged)",
             f"{'pr':<22} {'queued':<16} {'merged-in-replay':<16} {'min':>7} {'merged-in-history':<17} {'min-hist':>8} {'hist-by':<7}"]
    for r in rows:
        lines.append(f"{r[0]:<22} {r[1]:<16} {r[2]:<16} {r[3]:>7} {r[4]:<17} {r[5]:>8} {r[6]:<7}")
    return "\n".join(lines) + "\n"


def cmd_score(argv):
    candidate, trace, conflicts, verbose, keep = "", "", "history", False, False
    rest = list(argv)
    for i, a in enumerate(rest[:-1]):
        if a == "--candidate" and os.path.isdir(rest[i + 1]):
            others = rest[:i] + rest[i + 2:]
            if "--trace" not in others[:-1]:
                break
            j = others.index("--trace")
            return cmd_lander_score(others[:j] + others[j + 2:], rest[i + 1], others[j + 1])
    while rest:
        a = rest.pop(0)
        if a == "--candidate" and rest:
            candidate = rest.pop(0)
        elif a == "--trace" and rest:
            trace = rest.pop(0)
        elif a == "--conflicts" and rest:
            conflicts = rest.pop(0)
        elif a == "--verbose":
            verbose = True
        elif a == "--keep":
            keep = True
        else:
            print(f"cc-replay score: unexpected '{a}'", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    if not candidate or not trace or conflicts not in ("history", "files", "none"):
        print("cc-replay score --candidate PATH --trace FILE [--conflicts history|files|none] [--verbose] [--keep]", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    t = load_trace(trace)
    out, log, chatter = score(os.path.abspath(candidate), t, conflicts, verbose, keep)
    sys.stdout.write(out)
    if verbose:
        sys.stderr.write(log + "\n")
        sys.stderr.write("--- candidate output ---\n" + chatter)
    return 0


# ── the lander path: trace v3, today's core/lander driven on a virtual clock ────────────────────────────────
ARRIVE = ("queued", "again", "requeued", "handed-pushed")   # a request reached the lander's inbox
FULL_SUITE = ("check-sh",)       # a plan holding one of these is a full-suite PR (the lane's own FULL_CHECKS default)
REVIEW_CAP = 3600                # a verdict line further than this from the PR's last line is not one read's length
DEFAULT_REVIEW = 480
BLOCKED_MIN, BLOCKED_MAX = 60, 3600   # a gap in this range between a PR's last line and its check starting is a
                                      # slot wait; a longer one is a stalled lane (an older release), not a slot
HIST_SLOTS, HIST_LOAD_FACTOR = 3, 2   # the live admission's defaults, which history's box ran under


def kv_of(words):
    return dict(w.split("=", 1) for w in words if "=" in w)


def lander_events(path, until=0):
    """[(epoch, kind, 'repo#N', words)] from a lander queue.log: `stage` lines as 'stage:<name>', and the arrivals."""
    out = []
    try:
        f = open(path, errors="replace")
    except OSError:
        return out
    with f:
        for line in f:
            t, _, msg = line.rstrip("\n").partition("\t")
            e = epoch(t)
            w = msg.split()
            if not e or (until and e > until) or len(w) < 2 or not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+#\d+", w[1]):
                continue
            if w[0] == "stage" and len(w) >= 3:
                out.append((e, "stage:" + w[2], w[1], w[3:]))
            elif w[0] in ARRIVE:
                out.append((e, w[0], w[1], w[2:]))
    out.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])
    return out


def job_record(landq, repo, pr):
    """The job file the lander keeps for (repo, pr): live, or rest/ once it ended; {} when neither is there."""
    for p in (f"{landq}/{repo}-{pr}.json", f"{landq}/rest/{repo}-{pr}.json"):
        j = read_json(p)
        if isinstance(j, dict):
            return j
    return {}


def lander_trace(log, landq, since, until, repos=()):
    """A v3 trace from the lander's queue.log and job files. A PR is in it when its first `queued` falls inside
    [since, until]. arrivals: every request after that; seen: when history's lane first acted on each (its first
    stage line after it, the pick-up). A new head starts at each `requeued`, `handed-pushed` or later `queued`
    (someone pushed or asked again after a stop) and at each "the head moved" in the job file. Gates and verdicts
    are recorded against the head they ran on, in order. From the job file's holds: conflicts (head, when history
    first found it conflicting with main) and gone (when its branch could no longer be fetched)."""
    ev = lander_events(log, until)
    first, prs, left_out, blocked = {}, {}, set(), []
    for e, k, key, w in ev:
        if k == "queued":
            first.setdefault(key, e)
    for e, k, key, w in ev:
        repo, _, n = key.rpartition("#")
        if repos and repo not in repos:
            continue
        if key not in first or first[key] < since:
            if key in first and e >= since:   # in flight when the window opened: its lead time began before it
                left_out.add(key)
            continue
        p = prs.setdefault(key, {"repo": repo, "pr": int(n), "arrivals": [], "seen": [], "bumps": [], "_gates": [],
                                 "_verdicts": [], "merged": None, "_last": e, "_ended": False})
        kv = kv_of(w)
        if k in ARRIVE:
            if k in ("requeued", "handed-pushed") or (k == "queued" and p["_ended"]):
                p["bumps"].append(e)
            p["arrivals"].append(e)
            p["seen"].append(0)
            p["_ended"] = False
        else:
            p["seen"] = [s or e for s in p["seen"]]   # every request still unseen was seen by this line
            p["_ended"] = k in ("stage:handback", "stage:query", "stage:done")
            if k == "stage:gate" and kv.get("gate"):
                p["_gates"].append((e, kv["gate"], int(kv.get("secs") or 0), kv.get("ok") or "no"))
                began = e - int(kv.get("secs") or 0)
                # after the lane's own `checking` (or a check before it) it sat waiting for a slot: all were busy
                if p.get("_lastk") in ("stage:checking", "stage:gate") and BLOCKED_MIN <= began - p["_last"] <= BLOCKED_MAX:
                    blocked.append([p["_last"], began])
            elif k == "stage:verdict" and kv.get("verdict"):
                p["_verdicts"].append((e, kv["verdict"], max(0, min(REVIEW_CAP, e - p["_last"]))))
            elif k == "stage:merged" and not p["merged"]:
                p["merged"] = {"at": e, "by": "person" if kv.get("by") == "before" else "lane"}
        p["_last"], p["_lastk"] = e, k
    gsecs, rsecs = {}, []
    for p in prs.values():
        p.pop("_last"), p.pop("_ended"), p.pop("_lastk")
        p["seen"] = [s or a for a, s in zip(p["arrivals"], p["seen"])]
        j = job_record(landq, p["repo"], p["pr"])
        holds = []
        for h in j.get("history") or []:
            at, why = epoch(h.get("at")), str(h.get("why") or "")
            if not at or at < p["arrivals"][0]:
                continue
            if why.startswith("the head moved"):
                p["bumps"].append(at)
            elif h.get("state") == "held":
                holds.append((at, why))
        p["bumps"] = sorted(set(p["bumps"]))
        idx = lambda t: sum(1 for b in p["bumps"] if b <= t)  # noqa: E731
        p["gates"] = {}
        for e, g, secs, ok in p.pop("_gates"):
            p["gates"].setdefault(g, []).append([idx(e), secs, ok, e])
        p["verdicts"] = [[idx(e), v, secs] for e, v, secs in p.pop("_verdicts")]
        p["conflicts"] = [list(c) for c in sorted({idx(at): at for at, why in reversed(holds) if " conflicts with " in why}.items())]
        p["gone"] = next((at for at, why in holds if "couldn't find remote ref" in why), 0)
        plan = j.get("plan") if isinstance(j.get("plan"), dict) else {}
        p["checks"] = list(plan.get("checks") or p["gates"])
        p["paid"] = bool(plan.get("paid")) if plan else bool(p["verdicts"])
        p["klass"] = plan.get("klass") or "leaf"
        p["files"] = list(j.get("files") or [])
        p["title"] = str(j.get("title") or "")
        p["opaque"] = not j and not p["gates"]   # history's lane never planned it: nothing says what it would run
        for g, runs in p["gates"].items():
            gsecs.setdefault(g, []).extend(r[1] for r in runs if r[2] == "yes")
        rsecs.extend(s for _, _, s in p["verdicts"])
    return {"version": 3, "kind": "lander", "since": stamp(since), "until": stamp(until), "extracted_at": stamp(time.time()),
            "left_out": sorted(left_out - set(prs)), "cores": os.cpu_count() or 1,
            "load": load_history(since, until), "blocked": blocked,
            "medians": {"gate": {g: int(median(v, 60)) for g, v in sorted(gsecs.items())},
                        "review": int(median(rsecs, DEFAULT_REVIEW))},
            "prs": sorted(prs.values(), key=lambda p: (p["arrivals"][0], p["repo"], p["pr"]))}


def main_red_spans(trace):
    """{check: [(from, to)]}: main is red on a check from the first main-red history recorded for it, on any PR, to
    the next time that check passed anywhere (the window's end when it never did). Red on main is the box's fact,
    not the PR's, so the replay asks the clock rather than the PR."""
    runs = {}
    for p in trace["prs"]:
        for g, rs in p["gates"].items():
            runs.setdefault(g, []).extend((r[3], r[2]) for r in rs if len(r) > 3)
    spans = {}
    for g, rs in runs.items():
        start = None
        for at, ok in sorted(rs):
            if ok == "main-red" and start is None:
                start = at
            elif ok == "yes" and start is not None:
                spans.setdefault(g, []).append((start, at))
                start = None
        if start is not None:
            spans.setdefault(g, []).append((start, epoch(trace["until"]) + 1))
    return spans


def load_history(since, until, where=""):
    """[[epoch, 1-minute load]] from sysstat's daily files (`sadf -d -- -q`), oldest first; [] when there are none.
    The lander halves its own slots on this number, so a replay without it runs a calmer box than history had."""
    where = where or os.environ.get("CC_REPLAY_SYSSTAT") or "/var/log/sysstat"
    out = []
    for f in sorted(glob.glob(f"{where}/sa[0-9][0-9]")):
        try:
            if os.path.getmtime(f) < since - 86400:
                continue
        except OSError:
            continue
        rc, text = sh(["sadf", "-d", f, "--", "-q"], timeout=60)
        for line in text.splitlines() if rc == 0 else []:
            c = line.split(";")
            if len(c) >= 6 and c[2].endswith(" UTC"):
                at = epoch(c[2][:-4].replace(" ", "T") + "Z")
                try:
                    if at and since - 900 <= at <= until:
                        out.append([at, float(c[5])])
                except ValueError:
                    pass
    return sorted(out)


def pctl(xs, q):
    """The nearest-rank q-quantile of xs (None when empty)."""
    xs = sorted(xs)
    return xs[max(0, min(len(xs) - 1, -int(-len(xs) * q // 1) - 1))] if xs else None


def full_suite(p):
    return any(c in FULL_SUITE for c in p.get("checks") or [])


def history_numbers(trace):
    """{key: queued→merged seconds} and the full-suite lane-seconds, as history recorded them."""
    lead, lane = {}, 0
    for p in trace["prs"]:
        if p["merged"]:
            lead[f"{p['repo']}#{p['pr']}"] = p["merged"]["at"] - p["arrivals"][0]
        if full_suite(p):
            lane += sum(r[1] for runs in p["gates"].values() for r in runs)
    return lead, lane


def replay_numbers(trace, log):
    """The same two numbers from the replay's own queue.log, read by the same parser as history's."""
    starts = {f"{p['repo']}#{p['pr']}": p["arrivals"][0] for p in trace["prs"]}
    full = {f"{p['repo']}#{p['pr']}" for p in trace["prs"] if full_suite(p)}
    lead, lane, gates, reads = {}, 0, 0, 0
    for e, k, key, w in lander_events(log):
        if k == "stage:merged" and key in starts and key not in lead:
            lead[key] = e - starts[key]
        elif k == "stage:gate":
            gates += 1
            if key in full:
                lane += int(kv_of(w).get("secs") or 0)
        elif k == "stage:verdict":
            reads += 1
    return lead, lane, gates, reads


def candidate_core(path):
    """The directory holding the candidate's `lander` package: PATH itself, PATH/core, or PATH's parent."""
    path = os.path.abspath(path)
    for d in (path, f"{path}/core", os.path.dirname(path)):
        if os.path.isfile(f"{d}/lander/lane.py"):
            return d
    raise SystemExit(f"cc-replay: {path} holds no lander package (core/lander/lane.py)")


def sha(*parts):
    return hashlib.sha1("\0".join(map(str, parts)).encode()).hexdigest()


class WindowEnd(BaseException):
    """The clock passed the trace's end: the repo's replay stops there. A BaseException, so no `except Exception`
    of the candidate's takes it for a fault of its own."""


class VClock:
    """The one clock of a single-threaded replay: it moves forward only, every move delivers the arrivals due, and
    a move past `until` ends the repo's replay."""

    def __init__(self, now, until=0):
        self.now, self.hook, self.until = now, None, until

    def to(self, t):
        self.now = max(self.now, int(t))
        if self.until and self.now > self.until:
            raise WindowEnd()
        if self.hook:
            self.hook()


class VTime:
    """The `time` module a candidate module sees: wall clock, monotonic and sleep are the virtual clock's."""

    def __init__(self, clock):
        self._c = clock

    def time(self):
        return float(self._c.now)

    monotonic = time

    def sleep(self, s):
        self._c.to(self._c.now + max(0, s))

    def gmtime(self, s=None):
        return time.gmtime(self._c.now if s is None else s)

    def localtime(self, s=None):
        return time.localtime(self._c.now if s is None else s)

    def strftime(self, fmt, t=None):
        return time.strftime(fmt, self.localtime() if t is None else t)

    def __getattr__(self, n):
        return getattr(time, n)


class VFuture:
    def __init__(self, clock, at, value=None, exc=None):
        self.clock, self.at, self.value, self.exc = clock, at, value, exc

    def done(self):
        return self.at <= self.clock.now

    def result(self, timeout=None):
        if self.exc:
            raise self.exc
        return self.value


class VPool:
    """The lane's check pool: a submitted check is answered at once, waits for a box-wide slot as the real runner's
    flock does (LanderWorld.slot_start), and its future is done at that start + its secs."""

    def __init__(self, world):
        self.world = world

    def __enter__(self):
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *a):
        return False

    def submit(self, fn, *a, **kw):
        self.world.secs = 0
        try:
            v, x = fn(*a, **kw), None
        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — the lane reads it from the future, as from a real one
            v, x = None, e
        return VFuture(self.world.clock, self.world.slot_start(self.world.secs) + self.world.secs, v, x)


class VFutures:
    """The `concurrent.futures` lane.py sees. wait() moves the clock to the first finished check; with a timeout,
    to the first poll at or after the next thing a real lane would notice there (an arrival, a hold running out)."""
    FIRST_COMPLETED, ALL_COMPLETED, FIRST_EXCEPTION = "FIRST_COMPLETED", "ALL_COMPLETED", "FIRST_EXCEPTION"

    def __init__(self, world):
        self.world = world

    def ThreadPoolExecutor(self, *a, **kw):  # noqa: N802 — the name lane.py calls
        return VPool(self.world)

    def wait(self, fs, timeout=None, return_when=None):
        fs, clock = list(fs), self.world.clock
        done = {f for f in fs if f.done()}
        if not done and fs:
            t = min(f.at for f in fs)
            nxt = self.world.next_wake()
            if timeout and nxt is not None and nxt < t:
                t = min(t, clock.now + timeout * max(1, -(-(nxt - clock.now) // timeout)))
            clock.to(t)
            done = {f for f in fs if f.done()}
        return done, set(fs) - done


class Unit:
    """A lander unit made of plain functions (a module is what the lane expects; any attribute bag will do). A
    function it lacks is a ReplayLeak naming it: an AttributeError would be the lane's UnitFault, a held job and a
    quietly wrong score (#841's digest_of)."""

    def __init__(self, name, **fns):
        self.__dict__.update(fns, _name=name)

    def __getattr__(self, fn):
        if fn.startswith("__"):
            raise AttributeError(fn)
        raise ReplayLeak(f"cc-replay: the lane called {self._name}.{fn}, which LanderWorld.units does not answer")


class LanderWorld:
    """Everything outside the candidate's lane, answered from a v3 trace: GitHub, git, the manifest, the runner,
    the reviewer, the box's load, and the units after the merge. It makes no real call."""

    def __init__(self, trace, mods, clock, slots, root):
        self.trace, self.clock, self.slots, self.root = trace, clock, slots, root
        self.L, self.T, self.RUN, self.J = mods["lane"], mods["types"], mods["run"], mods["jobs"]
        self.GitError = mods["git"].GitError
        self.prs = {(p["repo"], p["pr"]): p for p in trace["prs"]}
        self.med = trace["medians"]
        self.main = {}        # repo -> [(sha, files, checks)] oldest first
        self.trees = {}       # main sha -> its tree
        self.merged = {}      # (repo, pr) -> the replay's merge time
        self.asks = {}        # (repo, pr, head, check or "review") -> times asked
        self.secs = 0
        self.lane = None
        self.repo = ""
        self.arrivals = []    # this repo's [(at, pr)] not yet delivered
        self.bought = 0
        self.red = main_red_spans(trace)
        self.A, self.at, self.own = mods["admission"], None, []
        self.held = sorted((r[3] - r[1], r[3], p["repo"]) for p in trace["prs"] for runs in p["gates"].values()
                           for r in runs if len(r) > 3 and r[1] > 0)   # history's box checks: (start, end, repo)

    # -- time and arrivals --
    def deliver(self):
        while self.arrivals and self.arrivals[0][0] <= self.clock.now:
            _, pr = self.arrivals.pop(0)
            self.J.submit(self.repo, pr, who="replay")

    def next_wake(self):
        """The next moment a lane polling this repo would find work: an arrival, or a hold running out on a job
        the running lane has not tried in this run."""
        ts = [self.arrivals[0][0]] if self.arrivals else []
        tried = self.lane.tried if self.lane else set()
        for j in self.J.lane_jobs(self.repo):
            if j.state == self.T.HELD and j.key not in tried:
                left = self.J.not_before_left(j, self.clock.now)
                ts.append(self.clock.now + max(1, left))
        return min(ts) if ts else None

    def slot_start(self, secs):
        """When a check asked for now gets its box-wide slot, as the runner's flock would give it: the first moment
        the checks in flight (history's in the other repos, the replay's own in this one) are fewer than the
        candidate's own slots_now() then, which reads history's load. The check holds its slot for its secs."""
        now = self.clock.now
        busy = [iv for iv in self.own if iv[1] > now]
        busy += [(a, b) for a, b, r in self.held if b > now and a <= now + 86400 and r != self.repo]
        loads = [at for at, _ in self.trace.get("load") or [] if at > now][:48]
        ends = [b for a, b in self.trace.get("blocked") or [] if b > now and a <= now + 86400]
        start = max([b for _, b in busy] + ends or [now])
        for t in sorted({now, *(b for _, b in busy), *loads, *ends}):
            if sum(1 for a, b in busy if a <= t < b) + self.phantom(t) < self.cap(t):
                start = t
                break
        if secs > 0:
            self.own.append((start, start + secs))
        return start

    def phantom(self, t):
        """Slots busy at t with work the trace never saw (a worker's own check run holds the same flocks): while a
        history check sat waiting, every one of history's slots was taken, so those its own checks did not fill
        were someone else's. 0 outside such a wait. The replay's lane asks a moment sooner than history's did (no real
        planning time), so a wait counts from BLOCKED_MIN before history's `checking` line."""
        if not any(a - BLOCKED_MIN <= t < b for a, b in self.trace.get("blocked") or []):
            return 0
        l1 = None
        for at, v in self.trace.get("load") or []:
            if at > t:
                break
            l1 = v
        cap = 1 if l1 is not None and l1 >= HIST_LOAD_FACTOR * (self.trace.get("cores") or 1) else HIST_SLOTS
        return max(0, cap - sum(1 for a, b, _ in self.held if a <= t < b))

    def cap(self, t):
        self.at = t
        try:
            return self.A.slots_now()
        finally:
            self.at = None

    # -- git and GitHub --
    def repo_of(self, root):
        return os.path.basename(root.rstrip("/"))

    def head_idx(self, p):
        return sum(1 for b in p["bumps"] if b <= self.clock.now)

    def head(self, repo, pr):
        p = self.prs.get((repo, pr))
        return sha(repo, pr, "head", self.head_idx(p) if p else 0)

    def pr_of_head(self, repo, h):
        for (r, n), p in self.prs.items():
            if r == repo and h == sha(r, n, "head", self.head_idx(p)):
                return p
        for (r, n), p in self.prs.items():
            if r == repo and any(h == sha(r, n, "head", i) for i in range(len(p["bumps"]) + 1)):
                return p
        return None

    def tip(self, repo):
        m = self.main.setdefault(repo, [(sha(repo, "main", 0), [], [])])
        return m[-1][0]

    def rev(self, root, ref, env=None):
        repo = self.repo_of(root)
        name = ref.rsplit("/", 1)[-1]
        m = re.fullmatch(r"pr-(\d+)", name)
        return self.head(repo, int(m.group(1))) if m else self.tip(repo)

    def between(self, repo, a, b):
        """The main entries after a, up to and including b."""
        m = self.main.get(repo) or []
        shas = [x[0] for x in m]
        ia = shas.index(a) if a in shas else -1
        ib = shas.index(b) if b in shas else len(m) - 1
        return m[ia + 1:ib + 1]

    def changed(self, root, a, b, env=None):
        repo = self.repo_of(root)
        p = self.pr_of_head(repo, b)
        if p:
            return list(p["files"]) or [f"?{p['pr']}"]
        return sorted({f for _, files, _ in self.between(repo, a, b) for f in files})

    def merge_tree(self, root, base, head, env=None):
        """Conflicting from the moment history first found this head conflicting until a new head: the rebase is a
        person's, so it comes when it came."""
        p = self.pr_of_head(self.repo_of(root), head)
        if p and any(i == self.head_idx(p) and at <= self.clock.now for i, at in p.get("conflicts") or []):
            return None, list(p["files"][:1]) or ["?"]
        return sha("tree", base, head), []

    def fetch(self, root, *branches, env=None):
        """{branch: sha} as G.fetch reports what origin sent (a lander that reads origin/<b> afterwards ignores it)."""
        repo = self.repo_of(root)
        for b in branches:
            m = re.fullmatch(r"pr-(\d+)", b or "")
            p = self.prs.get((repo, int(m.group(1)))) if m else None
            if p and p.get("gone") and p["gone"] <= self.clock.now:
                raise self.GitError(f"couldn't find remote ref refs/heads/{b}")
        return {b: self.rev(root, b) for b in branches if b}

    def tree_of(self, root, commit, env=None):
        return self.trees.get(commit) or sha("tree", commit)

    def pr_facts(self, root, pr, fields, token=None, timeout=120):
        repo = self.repo_of(root)
        p = self.prs.get((repo, int(pr))) or {}
        person = (p.get("merged") or {}).get("by") == "person" and p["merged"]["at"] <= self.clock.now
        state = "MERGED" if (repo, int(pr)) in self.merged or person else "OPEN"
        return {"state": state, "isDraft": bool(p.get("opaque")) and state == "OPEN", "mergeable": "MERGEABLE", "headRefOid": self.head(repo, int(pr)),
                "headRefName": f"pr-{pr}", "baseRefName": "main", "title": p.get("title") or f"PR {pr}",
                "body": ""}, ""

    def merge_state(self, root, pr, token=None):
        repo = self.repo_of(root)
        return ("MERGED", self.tip(repo)) if (repo, int(pr)) in self.merged else ("OPEN", "")

    def merge(self, root, pr, pin, title, token=None):
        repo = self.repo_of(root)
        before = self.tip(repo)
        p = self.prs.get((repo, int(pr))) or {"files": [], "checks": [], "pr": pr}
        new = sha(repo, "main", len(self.main[repo]), pr)
        self.main[repo].append((new, list(p["files"]) or [f"?{pr}"], list(p.get("checks") or [])))
        self.trees[new] = sha("tree", before, pin)
        self.merged[(repo, int(pr))] = self.clock.now
        return True, "merged"

    # -- the units --
    def plan(self, root, base, head, files, fallback=""):
        repo = self.repo_of(root)
        p = self.pr_of_head(repo, head)
        if p:
            return self.T.Plan(checks=list(p["checks"]), paid=bool(p["paid"]), klass=p.get("klass") or "leaf",
                               owned=list(files))
        seen = []   # a range of main: the checks the PRs merged in it planned
        for _, _, checks in self.between(repo, base, head):
            seen += [c for c in checks if c not in seen]
        return self.T.Plan(checks=seen, owned=list(files))

    def load1(self, *a, **k):
        """History's 1-minute load at this moment (the last sample before it), scaled to this machine's cores so the
        candidate's own overloaded() reads it as history's box did; None (calm) when history recorded none."""
        got, now = None, self.clock.now if self.at is None else self.at
        for at, l1 in self.trace.get("load") or []:
            if at > now:
                break
            got = l1
        return None if got is None else got * (os.cpu_count() or 1) / (self.trace.get("cores") or 1)

    def ask(self, *key):
        self.asks[key] = self.asks.get(key, 0) + 1
        return self.asks[key] - 1

    def run_plan(self, root, m, plan, files, tree, base_tree="", *, only=(), **kw):
        repo, T, RUN = self.repo_of(root), self.T, self.RUN
        out = {}
        p = self.prs.get((repo, kw.get("pr"))) or {}
        for n in only or plan.checks:
            idx = self.head_idx(p) if p else 0
            runs = [r for r in (p.get("gates") or {}).get(n, []) if r[0] == idx and r[2] != "main-red"]
            red = next((r for r in (p.get("gates") or {}).get(n, []) if r[2] == "main-red"), None)
            if any(a <= self.clock.now < b for a, b in self.red.get(n, [])):
                secs, ok = (red[1] if red else self.med["gate"].get(n, 60)), "main-red"
            elif runs:
                _, secs, ok = runs[min(self.ask(repo, p.get("pr"), idx, n), len(runs) - 1)][:3]
            else:
                secs, ok = self.med["gate"].get(n, 60), "yes"
            status = {"yes": T.PASSED, "main-red": RUN.BLOCKED}.get(ok, T.FAILED)
            res = T.Result(check=n, tree=tree, status=T.PASSED if ok == "yes" else T.FAILED, secs=float(secs))
            out[n] = RUN.Outcome(n, status, "main-red" if ok == "main-red" else "", [res])
            self.secs += secs
        return out

    def review(self, job, prior=None):
        T = self.T
        p = self.prs.get((job.repo, job.pr)) or {}
        idx = self.head_idx(p) if p else 0
        mine = [v for v in p.get("verdicts") or [] if v[0] == idx]
        k = self.ask(job.repo, job.pr, idx, "review")
        if mine:
            _, word, secs = mine[min(k, len(mine) - 1)]
        else:   # no read recorded at this head: the PR's last word, LAND when history merged it
            word = "LAND" if p.get("merged") or not p.get("verdicts") else p["verdicts"][-1][1]
            secs = self.med["review"]
        self.clock.to(self.clock.now + secs)
        word = word if word in (T.LAND, T.HANDBACK_VERDICT, T.INCOMPLETE) else T.HANDBACK_VERDICT
        self.bought += 1
        return T.Verdict(verdict=word, digest=job.digest, model="replay", tokens=1,
                         blocking=["the review history recorded"] if word == T.HANDBACK_VERDICT else [])

    def units(self):
        none = lambda *a, **k: None  # noqa: E731
        fns = {"planner": dict(plan=self.plan), "runner": dict(run_plan=self.run_plan),
               "reviewer": dict(review=self.review, delta_review=self.review,
                                digest_of=lambda root, base, head: sha("digest", head)),   # review.digest_of runs git
               "cards": dict(stopped=none, landed=none), "board": dict(close=none),
               "deploy": dict(request=none), "tip": dict(kick=none)}
        return {k: Unit(k, **v) for k, v in fns.items()}


def cached_reader(read):
    """read(path), answered from memory while the file is the same one (inode, size, mtime): a lane re-reads every
    job file for each job it tries, which is most of a replay's time and none of its answer."""
    memo = {}

    def cached(path):
        try:
            st = os.stat(path)
        except OSError:
            return read(path)
        key = (st.st_ino, st.st_size, st.st_mtime_ns)
        hit = memo.get(path)
        if hit and hit[0] == key:
            return json.loads(hit[1])
        v = read(path)
        memo[path] = (key, json.dumps(v))
        return v
    return cached


def _digest_unit(core):
    """The reviewer unit a replay hands the lane, built the way lander_score builds it (selfcheck only)."""
    sys.path.insert(0, core)
    import importlib
    mods = {n: importlib.import_module(f"lander.{n}") for n in ("types", "events", "jobs", "git", "gh", "manifest",
                                                                 "run", "admission", "members", "records", "lane")}
    return LanderWorld({"prs": [], "medians": {"review": 1}, "until": "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z"}, mods, VClock(0, 1), 0,
                       tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-replay-digest-")).units()["reviewer"]


def stand_in(mods, world, clock):
    """Point the candidate's own module attributes at the world: what it calls outside itself, and its clock."""
    L, G, GH, MF, RUN, A, J, M = (mods[k] for k in ("lane", "git", "gh", "manifest", "run", "admission", "jobs", "members"))
    vt = VTime(clock)
    for m in mods.values():
        if getattr(m, "time", None) is time:
            m.time = vt
    L.futures = VFutures(world)
    G.fetch = world.fetch
    G.rev, G.tree_of, G.changed, G.merge_tree = world.rev, world.tree_of, world.changed, world.merge_tree
    G.pr_changed = world.changed   # a PR head's files are the PR's own, whatever the base
    G.merge_base = lambda root, a, b, env=None: a
    G.patch_digest = lambda root, base, head, env=None: sha("digest", head)
    G.remote_head = lambda root, branch, env=None: world.rev(root, branch)
    G.protected_same = lambda *a, **k: True
    G.git_lock = lambda root: contextlib.nullcontext()
    # history merged with no CI-green gate (#916 added it): no workflows, and world.pr_facts reports no checks, so
    # the candidate's own gh.ci_state reads "none" and the merge goes ahead as it did then
    G.has_workflows = lambda root, rev: False
    GH.pr_facts, GH.merge_state, GH.merge = world.pr_facts, world.merge_state, world.merge
    GH.backoff = lambda: 0
    MF.load = lambda *a, **k: MF.Manifest()
    MF.widen = lambda base, head: base
    MF.placed = lambda m, tip: m
    MF.host_fallback = lambda repo: ""
    RUN.laptop_dest, RUN.quarantine_text = (lambda: ""), (lambda root, rev: "")
    RUN.may_leave, RUN.laptop_gone = (lambda c: False), (lambda outs: False)
    A.load1, A.loaded = world.load1, (lambda *a, **k: False)
    if world.slots:
        A.SLOTS = world.slots
    J.stale_release = lambda: ""
    J.read_json = cached_reader(J.read_json)
    J.repo_root = lambda repo: f"{world.root}/dev/{repo}"
    M.route = lambda job: ""
    L.paused = lambda target: False
    L.tier_stop = lambda: False
    L.protected_rules = lambda repo: []
    L.Lane.unit = answering(L.Lane.unit)


def answering(unit):
    """Lane.unit, but a unit the world has none of is a ReplayLeak naming it, not the lane's UnitFault."""
    def answered(lane, name):
        u = unit(lane, name)
        if u is None:
            raise ReplayLeak(f"cc-replay: the lane asked for its {name} unit, which LanderWorld.units has none of")
        return u
    return answered


class ReplayLeak(BaseException):
    """A candidate lander call the replay does not answer: a unit function, a unit, or a real process. A
    BaseException, so the lane's `except Exception` cannot turn it into a held job and a quietly wrong score."""


SPAWNERS = ("run", "Popen", "call", "check_call", "check_output", "getoutput", "getstatusoutput")


@contextlib.contextmanager
def tripwire(core):
    """Refuse every process the candidate's lander starts while the block runs, naming the lander frames that led to
    it (outermost first) and the argv. The stand-ins are one function at a time, so a lander change that reaches git
    some new way would otherwise run real git against a directory that is no repo, and fail somewhere quieter."""
    here, real, seen = os.path.realpath(core) + "/lander/", {n: getattr(subprocess, n) for n in SPAWNERS}, {}

    def lander(fr):
        f = fr.f_code.co_filename
        if f not in seen:
            seen[f] = os.path.realpath(f).startswith(here)
        return seen[f]

    def guard(name):
        def spawn(*a, **k):
            chain, fr = [], sys._getframe(1)
            while fr is not None:
                if lander(fr):
                    chain.append(f"{os.path.basename(fr.f_code.co_filename)[:-3]}.{fr.f_code.co_name}:{fr.f_lineno}")
                fr = fr.f_back
            if not chain:
                return real[name](*a, **k)
            argv = a[0] if a else k.get("args", k.get("cmd", "?"))
            argv = " ".join(map(str, argv)) if isinstance(argv, (list, tuple)) else str(argv)
            raise ReplayLeak(f"cc-replay: an unstubbed lander call ran `{argv[:120]}`: {' > '.join(reversed(chain))}"
                             " — answer it in stand_in or LanderWorld.units")
        return spawn
    for n in SPAWNERS:
        setattr(subprocess, n, guard(n))
    try:
        yield
    finally:
        for n, f in real.items():
            setattr(subprocess, n, f)


def lander_score(candidate, trace, slots=0, keep_root=False, pickup="history"):
    """Drive the candidate lander tree through the trace, one repo at a time, and return (report, log)."""
    core = candidate_core(candidate)
    root = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-replay-lander-")
    os.environ.update(CC_LANDER_STATE=f"{root}/land", HOME=root, CC_DEV=f"{root}/dev", CC_BOARDS=f"{root}/boards",
                      CC_MEMBERS=f"{root}/members", CC_BIN=f"{root}/bin", TMPDIR=root)
    for d in ("land", "dev", "boards", "members", "bin"):
        os.makedirs(f"{root}/{d}", exist_ok=True)
    sys.path.insert(0, core)
    import importlib
    names = ("types", "events", "jobs", "git", "gh", "manifest", "run", "admission", "members", "records", "lane")
    mods = {n: importlib.import_module(f"lander.{n}") for n in names}
    if not os.path.realpath(mods["lane"].__file__).startswith(os.path.realpath(core) + "/"):
        raise SystemExit(f"cc-replay: `lander` imported from {mods['lane'].__file__}, not the candidate {core}")
    until = epoch(trace["until"])
    clock = VClock(0, until)
    world = LanderWorld(trace, mods, clock, slots, root)
    stand_in(mods, world, clock)
    os.fsync = lambda fd: None   # the replay's own temp files: durability buys nothing and costs most of the run
    try:
        with tripwire(core):
            log = drive(trace, mods, world, clock, root, pickup)
        lead, lane, gates, reads = replay_numbers(trace, f"{root}/land/queue.log")
        return lander_report(trace, candidate, slots, pickup, lead, lane, gates, reads), "\n".join(log)
    except ReplayLeak as e:
        raise SystemExit(str(e)) from None
    finally:
        if keep_root:
            print(f"cc-replay: kept {root}", file=sys.stderr)
        else:
            shutil.rmtree(root, ignore_errors=True)


def drive(trace, mods, world, clock, root, pickup):
    """Run the candidate's lane over each repo in the trace until the window ends; the lane's log lines."""
    log = []
    for repo in sorted({p["repo"] for p in trace["prs"]}):
        os.makedirs(f"{root}/dev/{repo}", exist_ok=True)
        world.repo, world.lane, world.own = repo, None, []
        world.arrivals = sorted((a, p["pr"]) for p in trace["prs"] if p["repo"] == repo
                                for a in (p["seen"] if pickup == "history" else p["arrivals"]))
        clock.now, clock.hook = world.arrivals[0][0], world.deliver
        try:
            while True:
                world.deliver()
                world.lane = mods["lane"].Lane(repo, world.units())
                log += world.lane.run()
                world.lane = None
                nxt = world.next_wake()
                if nxt is None:
                    break
                clock.to(nxt)
        except WindowEnd:
            log += world.lane.lines if world.lane else []
    return log


def mins(s):
    return "-" if s is None else f"{s / 60:.1f}"


def lander_report(trace, candidate, slots, pickup, lead, lane, gates, reads):
    hist, hlane = history_numbers(trace)
    both = sorted(set(hist) & set(lead))
    rp = [lead[k] for k in both]
    hp = [hist[k] for k in both]
    hgates = sum(len(r) for p in trace["prs"] for r in p["gates"].values())
    hreads = sum(len(p["verdicts"]) for p in trace["prs"])
    out = [f"score p50 {mins(pctl(rp, .5))} min  p95 {mins(pctl(rp, .95))} min  full-suite lane-min {lane / 60:.0f}"
           f"  (queued→merged over {len(both)} PRs both merged; slots {slots or 'the candidate\'s'}, pick-up {pickup})",
           f"history p50 {mins(pctl(hp, .5))} min  p95 {mins(pctl(hp, .95))} min  full-suite lane-min {hlane / 60:.0f}",
           f"merged: replay {len(lead)}, history {len(hist)} of {len(trace['prs'])} PRs; checks run: replay {gates}, "
           f"history {hgates}; reads: replay {reads}, history {hreads}; trace {trace['since']} → {trace['until']}",
           "", f"{'PR':<22} {'history':>8} {'replay':>8}"]
    for p in trace["prs"]:
        k = f"{p['repo']}#{p['pr']}"
        out.append(f"{k:<22} {mins(hist.get(k)):>8} {mins(lead.get(k)):>8}")
    return "\n".join(out) + "\n"


def cmd_lander_score(argv, candidate, trace_path):
    slots, verbose, keep, pickup = 0, False, False, "history"
    rest = list(argv)
    while rest:
        a = rest.pop(0)
        if a == "--slots" and rest and rest[0].isdigit():
            slots = max(1, int(rest.pop(0)))
        elif a == "--pickup" and rest and rest[0] in ("history", "arrival"):
            pickup = rest.pop(0)
        elif a == "--verbose":
            verbose = True
        elif a == "--keep":
            keep = True
        else:
            print(f"cc-replay score: unexpected '{a}' for a lander tree", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    t = load_trace(trace_path)
    if t.get("kind") != "lander":
        print("cc-replay score: a lander tree scores a v3 trace (`cc-replay extract --lander`)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    out, log = lander_score(candidate, t, slots, keep, pickup)
    sys.stdout.write(out)
    if verbose:
        sys.stderr.write(log + "\n")
    return 0


# ── selfcheck ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def fixture_trace(n=4, t0=1_800_000_000, stopped=(), recorded_at=0, version=1, person=(), behind=()):
    """n PRs on disjoint files, queued a minute apart, each with its own gate durations; PR 2 and 3 share a file.
    A PR in `stopped` bought a DO-NOT-LAND on its head; with `recorded_at`, a person recorded LAND on it that many
    seconds after it was queued. v2 only: a PR in `person` was merged by hand at its history time, one in `behind`
    was stopped merely behind."""
    landings = []
    for i in range(1, n + 1):
        files = [["M", f"bin/tool{i}"]] + ([["M", "bin/shared"]] if i in (2, 3) else [])
        landings.append({"repo": "r", "pr": i, "title": f"change {i}", "branch": f"track/t{i}", "base": "main",
                         "created": stamp(t0 - 600), "merged": stamp(t0 + 3600 * i), "state": "MERGED",
                         "files": files, "perfile": {p: [10, 2] for _, p in files}, "adds": 10, "dels": 2,
                         "arrivals": [{"at": stamp(t0 + 60 * i), "again": False}],
                         "heads": [{"at": stamp(t0 - 600), "sha": f"{i:012x}", "gen": 0, "via": "push"}],
                         "verdicts": [], "fixes": [], "dones": [], "gates": {"check.sh": 60, "selftest.sh": 300 * i},
                         "red": {}, "green": [], "tiers": [], "review_secs": [200], "attempts": 1, "conflicted": False,
                         "queue_merged": True})
        if i in stopped:
            landings[-1]["verdicts"] = [{"at": stamp(t0 + 60 * i + 200), "head": f"{i:012x}", "gen": 0, "kind": "bought",
                                         "verdict": "DO-NOT-LAND", "by": "claude-x", "cost": 1.0}]
            if recorded_at:
                landings[-1]["verdicts"].append({"at": stamp(t0 + 60 * i + recorded_at), "head": f"{i:012x}", "gen": 0,
                                                 "kind": "recorded", "verdict": "LAND", "by": "a person", "cost": 0.0})
        if version >= 2:
            landings[-1].update(memo=[], person={"at": stamp(t0 + 3600 * i)} if i in person else None,
                                queue_merged=i not in person,
                                stops=[{"at": stamp(t0 + 1800), "kind": "behind", "head": f"{i:012x}", "behind": 1}] if i in behind else [])
    return {"version": version, "since": stamp(t0), "until": stamp(t0 + 86400),
            "repos": {"r": {"default_branch": "main", "gates": ["tests/check.sh", "tests/selftest.sh"], "control": None}},
            "medians": {"gate": {"check.sh": 60, "selftest.sh": 600}, "review": 200, "fix": 900}, "landings": landings, "gaps": []}


def cmd_selfcheck():
    fails = []

    def check(name, cond):
        print(("  ✓ " if cond else "  ✗ ") + name)
        if not cond:
            fails.append(name)

    # 1. the virtual clock: four gate threads park for 100/200/300/400 s; joining them all takes the clock to +400
    #    and no wall-clock time, and each advance lands on a wake — never a tick between them.
    clock = Clock(1000)
    th = FakeThreading(clock)
    ends = []
    ts = [th.Thread(target=lambda d=d: (clock.sleep(d), ends.append(clock.now))) for d in (300, 100, 400, 200)]
    w0 = time.time()
    for t in ts:
        t.start()
    for t in ts:
        t.join()
    _t = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-replay-shim-")
    try:
        load_candidate(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "cc-la" + "nd"), _t, None, None, None)
        _said = ""
    except SystemExit as e:
        _said = str(e)
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(_t, ignore_errors=True)
    check("today's core/bin shim onto the lander is refused as a candidate, with one line saying why", NOT_MONOLITH in _said)
    check("virtual clock: four parked gate threads advance the clock to the longest (1400), in wake order, in no wall time",
          clock.now == 1400 and sorted(ends) == [1100, 1200, 1300, 1400] and time.time() - w0 < 2)
    check("…and it advanced exactly four times — once per distinct wake, never on a tick", clock.advances == 4)
    clock = Clock(0)
    th = FakeThreading(clock)
    same = [th.Thread(target=lambda: clock.sleep(300)) for _ in range(4)]
    for t in same:
        t.start()
    for t in same:
        t.join()
    check("…and four threads parked for the SAME 300 s advance it once, to 300", clock.now == 300 and clock.advances == 1)
    # Event and Condition park too: a waiter on an Event nobody has set is parked, and the clock still moves for
    # the sleeper beside it; the set wakes the waiter without a tick.
    clock = Clock(0)
    th = FakeThreading(clock)
    ev, got = th.Event(), []
    waiter = th.Thread(target=lambda: (ev.wait(), got.append(clock.now)))
    setter = th.Thread(target=lambda: (clock.sleep(50), ev.set()))
    waiter.start(); setter.start(); waiter.join(); setter.join()
    check("an Event waiter is parked, the sleeper beside it moves the clock to 50, and set() wakes the waiter there",
          got == [50] and clock.now == 50)
    clock = Clock(0)
    th = FakeThreading(clock)
    cv, box = th.Condition(), []
    def consumer():
        with cv:
            while not box:
                cv.wait()
            box.append(clock.now)
    def producer():
        clock.sleep(70)
        with cv:
            box.append("x")
            cv.notify_all()
    c, p = th.Thread(target=consumer), th.Thread(target=producer)
    c.start(); p.start(); c.join(); p.join()
    check("a Condition waiter is parked and wakes on notify at the producer's virtual time", box == ["x", 70])
    # Arrivals: an arrival due before the next wake is injected at its own time, with the clock stopped there.
    clock = Clock(0)
    th = FakeThreading(clock)
    seen = []
    clock.inject = lambda p: seen.append((p, clock.now))
    clock.arrivals = [(40, "a"), (90, "b")]
    t = th.Thread(target=lambda: clock.sleep(100))
    t.start(); t.join()
    check("arrivals due before a wake are injected at their own times, and the sleeper still wakes at 100",
          seen == [("a", 40), ("b", 90)] and clock.now == 100)
    # A deadlock — everything parked, nothing due — is reported, not hung.
    clock = Clock(0)
    th = FakeThreading(clock)
    ev2 = th.Event()
    dead = []
    t = th.Thread(target=lambda: (lambda: dead.append(ev2.wait()))())
    t.start()
    try:
        t.join()
    except Deadlock:
        dead.append("raised")
    check("every thread parked with nothing due is a Deadlock raised to the joiner, never a hang", "raised" in dead and clock.dead)

    # 2. the conflict model: a PR conflicts when a PR merged since its base, in the replay's order, touches one of
    #    its files — and not when the files are disjoint, and not once it has rebased past that merge.
    tr = fixture_trace()
    root = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-replay-selfcheck-")
    try:
        w = World(tr, root, Clock(0), "files")
        w.merges.append((0, "r", 2, 0, {"bin/tool2", "bin/shared"}))
        check("conflict model: PR 3 (shares bin/shared) conflicts after PR 2 merged past its base", w.conflicting(("r", 3)))
        check("…and PR 4, on disjoint files, does not", not w.conflicting(("r", 4)))
        w.rebase(("r", 3))
        check("…and a rebase past that merge clears it", not w.conflicting(("r", 3)))
        w.merges.append((1, "r", 4, 0, {"bin/tool4"}))
        check("…a later merge on other files leaves it clear", not w.conflicting(("r", 3)))
        w2 = World(tr, root, Clock(0), "none")
        w2.merges.append((0, "r", 2, 0, {"bin/shared"}))
        check("--conflicts none never conflicts", not w2.conflicting(("r", 3)))
        w4 = World(tr, root, Clock(0), "history")
        w4.merges.append((0, "r", 2, 0, {"bin/shared"}))
        w4.prs[("r", 3)]["conflicted"] = True
        check("--conflicts history (the default) conflicts a PR history saw conflict, on the same rule…",
              w4.conflicting(("r", 3)))
        w4.prs[("r", 3)]["conflicted"] = False
        check("…and never one history did not", not w4.conflicting(("r", 3)))
        # the gh answer carries it: mergeable flips to CONFLICTING, and a merge is refused with GitHub's words
        w3 = World(tr, root, Clock(0), "files")
        w3.merges.append((0, "r", 2, 0, {"bin/shared"}))
        cwd = f"{root}/dev/r"
        rc, o = w3.gh(["gh", "pr", "view", "3", "--json", "state,mergeable"], cwd)
        check("gh pr view answers CONFLICTING for it", rc == 0 and json.loads(o)["mergeable"] == "CONFLICTING")
        rc, o = w3.gh(["gh", "pr", "merge", "3", "--squash"], cwd)
        check("…and gh pr merge refuses it with GitHub's own words", rc == 1 and "merge conflicts" in o)
        rc, o = w3.gh(["gh", "pr", "merge", "4", "--squash"], cwd)
        rc2, o2 = w3.gh(["gh", "pr", "view", "4", "--json", "state,mergedAt"], cwd)
        check("a clean PR merges and reads MERGED after", rc == 0 and json.loads(o2)["state"] == "MERGED")
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(root, ignore_errors=True)

    # 3. the trace loader: a fixture round-trips through a file, and a file that is not a trace is refused.
    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-replay-selfcheck-")
    try:
        with open(f"{d}/t.json", "w") as f:
            json.dump(fixture_trace(), f)
        t = load_trace(f"{d}/t.json")
        check("trace loader: a fixture loads with its landings, arrivals, heads and medians",
              len(t["landings"]) == 4 and t["landings"][2]["files"][1][1] == "bin/shared" and t["medians"]["review"] == 200)
        with open(f"{d}/bad.json", "w") as f:
            f.write('{"version": 2}')
        try:
            load_trace(f"{d}/bad.json")
            bad = False
        except SystemExit:
            bad = True
        check("…and a file that is not a v1 or v2 trace is refused", bad)
        # the ledger and marker readers, on lines of the shapes the sources print
        ev = ledger_events_from_text("2026-09-07T10:00:00Z\tqueued r#7 who=- chat=- by=x\n2026-09-07T10:30:00Z\tdone r#7 rc=0 [r] PR #7: landed ✅\n"
                                     "2026-09-07T10:31:00Z\tqueued r#deploy span=a..b by=the catch-up sweep\n", 0, 2_000_000_000)
        check("the ledger reader keeps queued/done for a PR and drops the deploy rows",
              [e["kind"] for e in ev] == ["queued", "done"] and ev[1]["rest"].startswith("rc=0"))
        old = parse_marker("<!-- cc-land-review 926d8b229822 LAND-AFTER-FIX -->\n**cc-land review** — `926d8b229822`, model `claude-opus-5`\n")
        new = parse_marker("<!-- cc-land-review v2 change=6eeebb3b7c8ccece3c98ae8111b83bc5045fd33d base=275f737a49f3 head=418892988b79 verdict=LAND by=r-b8-reviewer -->\nx")
        check("both marker shapes are read: the head-keyed one is a bought verdict, the change-keyed one signed by a "
              "person is a recorded one", old == ("926d8b229822", "LAND-AFTER-FIX", "", "claude-opus-5", "bought")
              and new == ("418892988b79", "LAND", "6eeebb3b7c8ccece3c98ae8111b83bc5045fd33d", "r-b8-reviewer", "recorded"))
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(d, ignore_errors=True)

    # 4. determinism, end to end: the OLD single-file tool scores the fixture twice to the same bytes, every PR
    #    merges, and the PRs on a shared file were gated one after the other (the second's merge is later). The file
    #    beside this one is a shim onto the lander now, so these run only on a copy CC_REPLAY_CANDIDATE names
    #    (`cc-bin-at <ref>` from before the cutover), and say they were skipped otherwise.
    cand = os.environ.get("CC_REPLAY_CANDIDATE") or os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "cc-land")
    try:
        monolith = "def cmd_work(" in open(cand, errors="replace").read()
    except OSError:
        monolith = False
    if not monolith:
        print("  - end-to-end scoring skipped: no old single-file landing tool here (CC_REPLAY_CANDIDATE names one)")
    if monolith:
        a, la, ca = score(cand, fixture_trace(), verbose=True)
        b, _, _ = score(cand, fixture_trace())
        check("determinism: two scores of the fixture trace against the cc-land beside this file are byte-identical", a == b)
        check("…and every fixture PR merged in the replay", "merged=4/4" in a.splitlines()[0])
        first = a.splitlines()[0]
        check("…with the score line in its contract shape", re.match(r"^score \d+\.\d suites=\d+ reviews=\d+ repairs=\d+ unmerged=\d+ merged=\d+/\d+$", first) is not None)
        r, lr, _ = score(cand, fixture_trace(stopped=(1,), recorded_at=900), verbose=True)
        check("a LAND a person recorded after the bought review stopped PR 1 lands it — queued again by the record, read, not bought again",
              "merged=4/4" in r.splitlines()[0] and "reviews=4" in r.splitlines()[0] and "after the recorded LAND" in lr)
        u, _, _ = score(cand, fixture_trace(stopped=(1,)))
        check("…and without the record the same PR stays open on its DO-NOT-LAND", "merged=3/4" in u.splitlines()[0])
        if not (a == b and "merged=4/4" in first):
            print(la[-3000:]); print(ca[-3000:])
        check("…and a v1 trace's report names no v2 counts", "trace=v2" not in a.splitlines()[1])
        # v2, end to end. A person's hand merge: PR 1 stopped on its DO-NOT-LAND merges at the time a person
        # merged it in history…
        p2, _, _ = score(cand, fixture_trace(version=2, stopped=(1,), person=(1,)))
        check("v2 person: a PR stopped in the replay is merged at its hand-merge time, counted as the person's",
              "merged=4/4" in p2.splitlines()[0] and "person-merged=1" in p2.splitlines()[1])
        # …a PR the candidate lands before that time stays the candidate's…
        p3, _, _ = score(cand, fixture_trace(version=2, person=(4,)))
        check("…a hand-merged PR the candidate lands first is not a person's merge", "person-merged=0" in p3.splitlines()[1])
        # …and the same stop on a v1 trace stays open, as it always did.
        p1, _, _ = score(cand, fixture_trace(version=1, stopped=(1,), person=(1,)))
        check("…and a v1 trace never merges it", "merged=3/4" in p1.splitlines()[0])
    else:
        print("  · no cc-land beside this file — the end-to-end cases did not run")

    # 5. trace v2's plumbing, behind stops and extraction, each on a fixture of its own.
    root = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-replay-selfcheck-")
    try:
        cwd = f"{root}/dev/r"
        w = World(fixture_trace(version=2), root, Clock(0), "history")
        g = lambda *a: w.git(["git", *a], cwd)
        tip0 = g("rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", "origin/main^{commit}")[1].strip()
        check("v2 plumbing: a head on an unmoved base holds it (is-ancestor rc 0), so merge_result gates the head",
              g("merge-base", "--is-ancestor", tip0, "3".zfill(12) + "0" * 28)[0] == 0)
        proj = g("commit-tree", g("merge-tree", "--write-tree", "1".zfill(12), "3".zfill(12))[1].strip(), "-p", "1".zfill(12), "-p", "3".zfill(12))[1].strip()
        projected = g("merge-tree", "--write-tree", proj, "4".zfill(12))[1].strip()
        w.clock.now = 10
        w.land(("r", 1)); w.land(("r", 3))
        tip = g("rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", "origin/main^{commit}")[1].strip()
        check("…once PR 1 merged past it, the base is no ancestor (rc 1) and the tip is a new commit",
              tip != tip0 and g("merge-base", "--is-ancestor", tip, "4".zfill(12))[0] == 1)
        check("…the merge of the base with PR 4, once 1 and 3 merged, is the very tree the projection gated",
              g("merge-tree", "--write-tree", tip, "4".zfill(12))[1].strip() == projected)
        w2 = World(fixture_trace(version=2), root, Clock(0), "history")
        w2.clock.now = 10
        w2.land(("r", 1))
        tip1 = w2.git(["git", "rev-parse", "origin/main^{commit}"], cwd)[1].strip()
        check("…and when PR 3 did not merge, it is another tree",
              w2.git(["git", "merge-tree", "--write-tree", tip1, "4".zfill(12)], cwd)[1].strip() != projected)
        v1w = World(fixture_trace(version=1), root, Clock(0), "history")
        v1w.merges.append((0, "r", 1, 0, {"bin/tool1"}))
        check("…while a v1 world answers as it always did: every head holds the base",
              v1w.git(["git", "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", "x", "4".zfill(12)], cwd)[0] == 0)
        # behind: PR 3 history saw stopped merely behind is refused once a merge passed its base; PR 4 is not.
        wb = World(fixture_trace(version=2, behind=(3,)), root, Clock(1_800_000_000), "history")
        wb.land(("r", 1))
        rc, o = wb.gh(["gh", "pr", "merge", "3", "--squash"], cwd)
        view = json.loads(wb.gh(["gh", "pr", "view", "3", "--json", "mergeStateStatus"], cwd)[1])
        check("v2 behind: a PR history stopped behind is refused with GitHub's --auto words while a merge passed its base",
              rc == 1 and "--auto" in o and view["mergeStateStatus"] == "BEHIND" and wb.n["behind"] == 1)
        check("…and a PR history never saw stopped merges though just as behind", wb.gh(["gh", "pr", "merge", "4", "--squash"], cwd)[0] == 0)
        old_head = wb.head(("r", 3))[0]
        rc, o = wb.gh(["gh", "pr", "update-branch", "3"], cwd)
        new_head, gen = wb.head(("r", 3))
        check(f"…gh pr update-branch merges the base in: a new head, the same change, {UPDATE_SECS} s on the clock, and it merges",
              rc == 0 and new_head != old_head and gen == 0 and wb.clock.now == 1_800_000_000 + UPDATE_SECS
              and wb.behind(("r", 3)) == 0 and wb.gh(["gh", "pr", "merge", "3", "--squash"], cwd)[0] == 0)
        wv1 = World(fixture_trace(version=1), root, Clock(0), "history")
        wv1.land(("r", 1))
        wv1.prs[("r", 3)]["stops"] = [{"kind": "behind", "behind": 1}]
        check("…and a v1 world neither refuses it nor answers update-branch",
              wv1.gh(["gh", "pr", "update-branch", "3"], cwd)[0] == 1 and wv1.gh(["gh", "pr", "merge", "3", "--squash"], cwd)[0] == 0)
        # extraction: the three classes read off lines of the shapes the sources print
        L = lambda at, pid, text: (at, pid, text)
        lines = [L(10, 7, "gating and reading 2 queued job(s) — side by side"),
                 L(11, 7, "  ✓ 1 gate(s) passed on PR #1 at the full tier (x): tests/check.sh"),
                 L(12, 7, "  ✓ 1 gate(s) passed on PR #2 at the full tier (x): tests/check.sh"),
                 L(13, 7, "  ✓ 1 gate(s) passed on PR #1: tests/check.sh — the full tier, x; run for this sweep by the prepare phase, on y"),
                 L(14, 7, "  ✓ 1 gate(s) passed on PR #2 at the full tier (x): tests/check.sh"),
                 L(20, 8, "  ✓ 1 gate(s) passed on PR #3 at the full tier (x): tests/check.sh"),
                 L(21, 8, "  ✓ 1 gate(s) passed on PR #3 at the full tier (x): tests/check.sh")]
        mf = memo_facts(lines, {("r", 1), ("r", 2), ("r", 3)})
        check("extract memo: a `by the prepare phase` line is a hit, gates passed twice in a prepared sweep a miss…",
              mf.get(("r", 1)) == [(13, True)] and mf.get(("r", 2)) == [(14, False)])
        check("…and twice in a sweep that prepared nothing is not a miss", ("r", 3) not in mf)
        tr = fixture_trace(person=(2,))
        tr["landings"][1]["queue_merged"] = False
        tr["landings"][0]["dones"] = [{"at": stamp(1_800_000_100), "rc": 1, "short": "[r] PR #1: NOT merged ❌ — PR #1 is not mergeable yet (checks pending, or it needs a rebase)"}]
        tr["landings"][2]["dones"] = [{"at": stamp(1_800_000_100), "rc": 1, "short": "[r] PR #3: NOT merged ❌ — PR #3 conflicts with main — rebase it, then land it"}]
        tr["landings"][3]["dones"] = [{"at": stamp(1_800_000_100), "rc": 1, "short": "[r] PR #4: NOT merged ❌ — gate tests/check.sh did not pass: a merge conflicts with x"}]
        counts = upgrade(tr, lines)
        by = {l["pr"]: l for l in tr["landings"]}
        check("extract stops: `not mergeable yet` is behind, `conflicts with main — rebase` a conflict, a red gate neither",
              [s["kind"] for s in by[1]["stops"]] == ["behind"] and [s["kind"] for s in by[3]["stops"]] == ["conflict"]
              and by[4]["stops"] == [] and by[3]["conflicted"] and not by[1]["conflicted"])
        check("extract person: a PR merged outside the queue carries its merge time, a queue merge none",
              by[2]["person"] == {"at": by[2]["merged"]} and by[1]["person"] is None)
        check("…and the trace names its version and the counts it printed",
              tr["version"] == 2 and counts == {"memo_hits": 1, "memo_misses": 1, "stops_behind": 1, "stops_conflict": 1, "person": 1})
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(root, ignore_errors=True)
    # the change key is the landing's own: a rebase that only moved a hunk's line numbers and its function-context
    # tail is one change, and a head keyed by a legacy (tail-kept) marker still matches its v2-keyed rebase.
    # The landing's own is the lander's review.change_digest now (core/lander/review.py, beside this file's bin/).
    core = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
    if core not in sys.path:
        sys.path.insert(0, core)
    import lander.review as land
    d1 = "diff --git a/x b/x\nindex 1..2 100644\n@@ -10,3 +10,4 @@ def f():\n a\n+b\n c\n"
    d2 = "diff --git a/x b/x\nindex 3..4 100644\n@@ -40,3 +40,4 @@ def g():\n a\n+b\n c\n"
    d3 = d2.replace("+b", "+z")
    check("replay digest: equals the landing's for the same diff, both rules",
          change_digest(d1) == land.change_digest(d1) and change_digest(d1, True) == land.change_digest(d1, legacy=True))
    check("…a rebase that moved only the hunk's numbers and tail is one change, under the v2 rule only",
          change_digest(d1) == change_digest(d2) and change_digest(d1, True) != change_digest(d2, True))
    check("…a legacy-keyed head and its v2-keyed rebase share a key; a changed body shares none",
          same_change((change_digest(d1, True), change_digest(d1), change_digest(d1, True)),
                      (change_digest(d2), change_digest(d2), change_digest(d2, True)))
          and not same_change((change_digest(d1, True), change_digest(d1), change_digest(d1, True)),
                              (change_digest(d3), change_digest(d3), change_digest(d3, True))))
    # the lander path (v3): a fixture queue.log and job files -> a trace; the trace -> this checkout's own lander,
    # driven in a child process (a candidate is imported as the `lander` package, once per process).
    t0 = 1_800_000_000
    lroot = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-replay-lander-fx-")
    try:
        lq = f"{lroot}/land"
        os.makedirs(f"{lq}/rest")
        L = lambda at, text: f"{stamp(t0 + at)}\t{text}\n"  # noqa: E731
        log = "".join([
            L(-100, "queued r#9 who=x"), L(5, "stage r#9 merged sha=aa"),
            L(10, "queued r#1 who=x"), L(11, "stage r#1 lane"), L(611, "stage r#1 gate gate=a ok=yes secs=600"),
            L(620, "stage r#1 merged sha=bb"), L(700, "stage r#1 done"),
            L(20, "queued r#2 who=x"), L(21, "stage r#2 lane"), L(621, "stage r#2 gate gate=b ok=yes secs=600"),
            L(700, "stage r#2 verdict verdict=LAND"), L(710, "stage r#2 merged sha=cc"),
            L(30, "queued r#3 who=x"), L(31, "stage r#3 lane"), L(1230, "stage r#3 gate gate=a ok=no secs=600"),
            L(1231, "stage r#3 handback"), L(2000, "requeued r#3 who=x"), L(2001, "stage r#3 lane"),
            L(2601, "stage r#3 gate gate=a ok=yes secs=600"), L(2700, "stage r#3 merged sha=dd"),
            L(40, "queued r#4 who=x"), L(3000, "stage r#4 merged by=before"),
            L(50, "stage demo#7 verdict=LAND digest=x"),
        ])
        with open(f"{lq}/queue.log", "w") as f:
            f.write("".join(sorted(log.splitlines(True))))
        for n, files, checks, paid, hist in ((1, ["x.py"], ["a"], False, []), (2, ["y.py"], ["b"], True, []),
                                              (3, ["x.py", "z.py"], ["a"], False,
                                               [{"at": stamp(t0 + 800), "state": "held", "why": "PR #3 conflicts with main: x.py"}])):
            with open(f"{lq}/rest/r-{n}.json", "w") as f:
                json.dump({"repo": "r", "pr": n, "files": files, "plan": {"checks": checks, "paid": paid}, "history": hist}, f)
        os.environ["CC_REPLAY_SYSSTAT"] = f"{lroot}/no-sysstat"
        tr = lander_trace(f"{lq}/queue.log", lq, t0, t0 + 4000)
        by = {p["pr"]: p for p in tr["prs"]}
        check("v3 extract: a PR first queued in the window is in, one queued before it is left out, a demo line is not a PR",
              sorted(by) == [1, 2, 3, 4] and tr["left_out"] == ["r#9"])
        check("…a request after a handback is a new head; the gates before it are head 0, after it head 1",
              by[3]["bumps"] == [t0 + 2000] and [r[:3] for r in by[3]["gates"]["a"]] == [[0, 600, "no"], [1, 600, "yes"]]
              and by[1]["bumps"] == [])
        check("…the pick-up is history's first stage line after each request; a verdict's secs run from the line before it",
              by[3]["seen"] == [t0 + 31, t0 + 2001] and by[4]["seen"] == [t0 + 3000] and by[2]["verdicts"] == [[0, "LAND", 79]])
        check("…a conflict hold from the job file is kept at its head; a PR the lane never planned is opaque, one it planned not",
              by[3]["conflicts"] == [[0, t0 + 800]] and by[4]["opaque"] and not by[1]["opaque"]
              and by[4]["merged"] == {"at": t0 + 3000, "by": "person"} and by[1]["merged"]["by"] == "lane")
        spans = main_red_spans({"until": stamp(1000), "prs": [{"gates": {"g": [[0, 5, "main-red", 100], [0, 5, "yes", 200]]}},
                                                                {"gates": {"g": [[0, 5, "main-red", 300]], "h": [[0, 5, "yes", 50]]}}]})
        check("main red is a span of time on any PR: to the next pass anywhere, or past the window's end; a pass alone is none",
              spans == {"g": [(100, 200), (300, 1001)]})
        calm = f"{lroot}/calm.json"
        with open(calm, "w") as f:
            json.dump(tr, f)
        me = os.path.realpath(__file__)

        def run(trace, *extra):
            r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, me, "score", "--candidate", core, "--trace", trace, *extra],
                               capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)
            rows = {ln.split()[0]: ln.split()[1:] for ln in r.stdout.splitlines()[5:] if ln.strip()}
            return r, rows
        a, arows = run(calm)
        b, _ = run(calm)
        num = lambda rows, k, i=1: float(rows[k][i]) if k in rows and rows[k][i] != "-" else None  # noqa: E731
        check("v3 score: a checkout's own core/lander is driven, and prints the score and history's line beside it",
              a.returncode == 0 and a.stdout.startswith("score p50 ") and "\nhistory p50 " in a.stdout)
        check("…the same trace scores to the same bytes", a.stdout == b.stdout and a.stdout)
        check("…a calm box runs #1's and #2's checks side by side: #2 merges ~11 min in, as history's recorded times say",
              num(arows, "r#2") is not None and 10.5 <= num(arows, "r#2") <= 12.0)
        check("…#3 shares x.py with #1, is handed back on its recorded red and merges on the head pushed after it",
              num(arows, "r#3") is not None and 42 <= num(arows, "r#3") <= 46)
        check("…a PR the lane never planned merges when the person merged it, not before",
              num(arows, "r#4") is not None and abs(num(arows, "r#4") - 49.3) < 0.2)
        check("…the reviewer's digest_of is answered from the trace (a stable stand-in per head), never by running git",
              (lambda u: u.digest_of("/nonexistent", "a", "h1") == u.digest_of("/nonexistent", "b", "h1")
               != u.digest_of("/nonexistent", "a", "h2"))(_digest_unit(core)))
        real_run, leak = subprocess.run, ""
        try:
            with tripwire(core):
                land.digest_of("/nonexistent", "a", "h1")
        except ReplayLeak as e:
            leak = str(e)
        check("…a lander call no stand-in answers is refused by name, not run: review.digest_of's git is a ReplayLeak",
              "review.digest_of:" in leak and "`git " in leak and subprocess.run is real_run)
        if a.returncode:
            print("    " + (a.stderr.strip().splitlines() or ["(no stderr)"])[-1])
        def leak_of(fn):
            try:
                fn()
            except ReplayLeak as e:
                return str(e)
            return ""
        check("…a unit function or a whole unit the world lacks is a ReplayLeak naming it, not a held job",
              "reviewer.nothing," in leak_of(lambda: _digest_unit(core).nothing)
              and "its tip unit" in leak_of(lambda: answering(lambda lane, name: None)(None, "tip")))
        check("…and a replay of this checkout's lander called nothing the world does not answer (the line above names it)",
              a.returncode == 0)
        # history's load reaches the candidate's own admission: three PRs side by side on a calm box, and on a box
        # at 2x its cores as many as the candidate's slots_now() admits at that load, the rest a check later
        tq = f"{lroot}/land-load"
        os.makedirs(f"{tq}/rest")
        with open(f"{tq}/queue.log", "w") as f:
            f.write("".join(sorted(L(at, f"{w} t#{n}{x}") for n in (1, 2, 3) for at, w, x in (
                (10, "queued", " who=x"), (11, "stage", " lane"), (611, "stage", f" gate gate=c{n} ok=yes secs=600"),
                (620, "stage", f" merged sha=t{n}")))))
        for n in (1, 2, 3):
            with open(f"{tq}/rest/t-{n}.json", "w") as f:
                json.dump({"repo": "t", "pr": n, "files": [f"t{n}.py"], "plan": {"checks": [f"c{n}"], "paid": False}}, f)
        lt = lander_trace(f"{tq}/queue.log", tq, t0, t0 + 4000)
        tcalm, tload = f"{lroot}/t-calm.json", f"{lroot}/t-load.json"
        with open(tcalm, "w") as f:
            json.dump(lt, f)
        with open(tload, "w") as f:
            json.dump(dict(lt, load=[[t0 - 900, 10_000.0]]), f)
        adm = importlib.import_module("lander.admission")
        with open(f"{lroot}/loadavg", "w") as f:
            f.write(f"{2 * (os.cpu_count() or 1) + 1} 1 1 1/1 1\n")
        want = adm.slots_now(f"{lroot}/no-psi", 3, f"{lroot}/loadavg")
        fast = lambda rows: sum(1 for n in (1, 2, 3) if (num(rows, f"t#{n}") or 99) < 12)  # noqa: E731
        (_, trows), (_, lrows) = run(tcalm, "--slots", "3"), run(tload, "--slots", "3")
        check(f"…history's load at 2x the cores reaches the candidate's slots_now() ({want} of 3): that many of three "
              "PRs merge in one check's time, the rest a check later; all three on a calm box",
              want < 3 and fast(trows) == 3 and fast(lrows) == want
              and all((num(lrows, f"t#{n}") or 0) >= 19 for n in range(want + 1, 4)))
        d, _ = run(calm, "--slots", "1")
        check("…--slots is the candidate's own SLOTS: one slot on a calm box is history's pace for #2 again",
              d.returncode == 0 and "slots 1," in d.stdout)
        # slot waits on work the trace never saw: its own fixture
        bq = f"{lroot}/land-blocked"
        os.makedirs(f"{bq}/rest")
        with open(f"{bq}/queue.log", "w") as f:
            f.write("".join(sorted([
                L(10, "queued s#5 who=x"), L(11, "stage s#5 lane"), L(12, "stage s#5 checking"),
                L(1212, "stage s#5 gate gate=a ok=yes secs=10"), L(1220, "stage s#5 merged sha=ee"),
                L(10, "queued s#6 who=x"), L(11, "stage s#6 lane"), L(1211, "stage s#6 gate gate=a ok=yes secs=10"),
                L(1300, "stage s#6 merged sha=ff"),
                L(10, "queued s#7 who=x"), L(12, "stage s#7 checking"), L(9212, "stage s#7 gate gate=a ok=yes secs=10"),
                L(9300, "stage s#7 merged sha=gg"),
            ])))
        for n in (5, 6, 7):
            with open(f"{bq}/rest/s-{n}.json", "w") as f:
                json.dump({"repo": "s", "pr": n, "files": [f"f{n}.py"], "plan": {"checks": ["a"], "paid": False}}, f)
        bt = lander_trace(f"{bq}/queue.log", bq, t0, t0 + 10000)
        check("v3 extract: a check that started 20 min after the lane's `checking` sat on a slot; one after a bare "
              "`lane` line, or 2.5 h later (a stalled lane), is no slot wait",
              bt["blocked"] == [[t0 + 12, t0 + 1202]])
        waits, free = f"{lroot}/waits.json", f"{lroot}/free.json"
        only5 = dict(bt, prs=[p for p in bt["prs"] if p["pr"] == 5])
        with open(waits, "w") as f:
            json.dump(only5, f)
        with open(free, "w") as f:
            json.dump(dict(only5, blocked=[]), f)
        (e, erows), (g, grows) = run(waits), run(free)
        check("v3 score: while history's check sat on a slot someone else held, the replay's waits it out too; "
              "without that wait it runs at once",
              num(erows, "s#5") is not None and num(erows, "s#5") >= 19.8 and num(grows, "s#5") is not None
              and num(grows, "s#5") < 2)
    finally:
        os.environ.pop("CC_REPLAY_SYSSTAT", None)
        shutil.rmtree(lroot, ignore_errors=True)
    print(f"cc-replay selfcheck: {len(fails)} failed")
    return 1 if fails else 0


def ledger_events_from_text(text, since, until):
    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-replay-ledger-")
    try:
        with open(f"{d}/queue.log", "w") as f:
            f.write(text)
        return ledger_events(f"{d}/queue.log", since, until)
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(d, ignore_errors=True)


def main(argv):
    if not argv or argv[0] in ("-h", "--help"):
        print(__doc__.strip().split("\n\n")[0] + "\n\n" + "\n".join(l for l in __doc__.splitlines() if l.startswith("  cc-replay ")))
        return 0 if argv else 2
    cmd, rest = argv[0], argv[1:]
    if cmd == "extract":
        return cmd_extract(rest)
    if cmd == "score":
        return cmd_score(rest)
    if cmd == "selfcheck":
        return cmd_selfcheck()
    print(f"cc-replay: unknown command '{cmd}'", file=sys.stderr)
    return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
